\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-\uc2 Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  leaves rates unchanged, uses  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  amid market turmoil\b0\par\par\uc2 566 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2023\par 09:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Benchmark rate left unchanged at 5.75%, as expected\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Headline inflation seen back to target from Sept 2023\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Further rate increases this year unlikely - analysts\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 BI governor says local banks resilient\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rupiah has been volatile\par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds quotes from governor, analysts)\par \par \uc2 By Gayatri Suroyo and Fransiska Nangoy\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, March 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has and will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market amid volatility linked to the closure of some U.S. banks, its governor said on Thursday, after leaving interest rates unchanged for a second straight meeting.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia (BI) \uc2 Governor \uc2 Perry Warjiyo\uc2  noted that the closure of three U.S. banks and problems at \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  have increased market uncertainty, halting capital flows to emerging markets and pressuring \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but he underlined that he saw no direct impact on local banks.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left unchanged its benchmark 7-day reverse repurchase rate at 5.75%, where it has been since January, as predicted by all 30 economists polled by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Seeking to reassure markets, the governor said based on BI's stress test local banks were resilient, with low non-performing loan and high capital adequacy ratios, as well as diverse funding sources.\par \par \uc2 "Our stress test assessment concluded that Indonesia's banking conditions are resilient to this impact and frankly we are continuing to monitor it," Warjiyo told a news conference.\par \par \uc2 Brushing off fears about a brewing global banking crisis, Warjiyo said President Joe Biden's measures would be enough to contain trouble in the U.S. banking sector.\par \par \uc2 He also said he did not think the collapse of some U.S. banks would affect the trajectory of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 However, BI would continue to watch market perceptions of global banking conditions, he said.\par \par \uc2 The governor reiterated that BI's rate hikes - totalling 225 basis points between August to January - were adequate to ensure headline inflation return to its target range starting in September, despite inflation picking up slightly in February to 5.47%.\par \par \uc2 To mitigate global risks, "we stabilise the rupiah. We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Warjiyo added.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah was little changed after the rate decision. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had dropped more than 0.5% against the dollar in early Thursday trading but regained some of the losses.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah and many other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been volatile in recent days as markets reacted to news of the collapse of the U.S. banks and its possible effect on the pace of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's monetary tightening.\par \par \uc2 Radhika Rao\uc2 , senior economist at \uc2 DBS Bank\uc2  in Singapore, said the decision to keep rates unchanged indicated BI's "confidence on the evolving inflation-growth path".\par \par \uc2 "The forward looking bias will be to keep rates on hold, albeit policy guidance could reflect a preference to stay nimble to backstop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in case of volatility in the global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," said Rao.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its 2023 growth outlook for Southeast Asia's largest economy at the upper end of a 4.5% to 5.3% range and a current account forecast range of between a deficit of 0.4% of gross domestic product to a surplus of 0.4% of GDP. (Reporting by Gayatri Suroyo, Fransiska Nangoy and Stefanno Sulaiman; Editing by Ed Davies, Martin Petty and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2023-3-16T09:53:46.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020230316ej3g018ai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
