                  is required. Accordingly, the \par                                                              Dealer agrees that it will observe \par                                                              all applicable provisions of law \par                                                              in each jurisdiction in or from \par                                                              which it may offer or sell Notes \par                                                              or distribute any offering material. \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recent Developments\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On November 20, 2022, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ilan Goldfajn\f28 \uc2 \f2  was elected president of the Bank during a Special Meeting of the Bank's Board of Governors. Mr. Goldfajn took office for a five-year term on December 19, 2022.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additional Information Regarding the Notes \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    1.         Matters relating to UK MiFIR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank does not fall under the scope of application of the UK MiFIR regime. Consequently, the Bank does not qualify as an "investment firm", "manufacturer" or "distributor" for the purposes of UK MiFIR.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UK MiFIR product governance / Retail investors, professional investors and ECPs target market - Solely for the purposes of the UK manufacturer's product approval process, the target market assessment in respect of the Notes has led to the conclusion that: (i) the target market for the Notes is retail clients, as defined in point (8) of Article 2 of Regulation (EU) No 2017/565 as it forms part of UK domestic law by virtue of the EUWA, eligible counterparties, as defined in COBS, and professional clients, as defined in UK MiFIR; and (ii) all channels for distribution of the Notes are appropriate. Any person subsequently offering, selling or recommending the Notes (a "distributor") should take into consideration the UK manufacturer's target market assessment; however, a distributor subject to the UK MiFIR Product Governance Rules is responsible for undertaking its own target market assessment in respect of the Notes (by either adopting or refining the UK manufacturer's target market assessment) and determining appropriate distribution channels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the purposes of this provision, (i) the expression "UK manufacturer" means the Dealer, (ii) the expression "COBS" means the \f28 \uc2 \f2 FCA\f28 \uc2 \f2  Handbook Conduct of Business Sourcebook, (iii) the expression "UK MiFIR" means Regulation (EU) No 600/2014 as it forms part of UK domestic law by virtue of the EUWA and (iv) the expression "UK MiFIR Product Governance Rules" means the \f28 \uc2 \f2 FCA\f28 \uc2 \f2  Handbook Product \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Product Governance Sourcebook. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.         Additional Investment Considerations: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Notes offered by this Pricing Supplement are complex financial instruments and may not be suitable for certain investors. Investors intending to purchase the Notes should consult with their tax and financial advisors to ensure that the intended purchase meets the investment objective before making such purchase.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are various risks associated with the Notes including, but not limited to, exchange rate risk, price risk and liquidity risk. Investors should consult with their own financial, legal and accounting advisors about the risks associated with an investment in these Notes, the appropriate tools to analyze that investment, and the suitability of the investment in each investor's particular circumstances. Holders of the Notes should also consult with their professional tax advisors regarding tax laws applicable to them.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment of each Interest Amount and the Redemption Amount will be based on the Reference Rate, which is a measure of the rate of exchange between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates are volatile and will affect the holder's return. In addition, the government of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can from time to time \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. These \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or other governmental actions could adversely affect the value of the Notes, as well as the yield (in USD terms) on the Notes and the amount payable at maturity or upon acceleration. Even in the absence of governmental action directly affecting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, political or economic developments in Indonesia or elsewhere could lead to significant and sudden changes in the exchange rate between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian Rupiah is an emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be subject to particularly substantial volatility, as well as to government actions including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls, devaluations and other matters which could materially and adversely affect the value of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The methodologies for determining the Reference Rate may result in a Redemption Amount (or Early Redemption Amount, as the case may be) of the Notes, or an Interest Amount on the Notes, being significantly less than anticipated or less than what an alternative methodology for determining the IDR-USD exchange rate would yield. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.         United Stated Federal Income Tax Matters: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following supplements the discussion under the "Tax Matters" section of the Prospectus regarding the U.S. federal income tax treatment of the Notes, and is subject to the limitations and exceptions set forth therein. Any tax disclosure in the Prospectus or this Pricing Supplement is of a general nature only, is not exhaustive of all possible tax considerations and is not intended to be, and should not be construed to be, legal, business or tax advice to any particular prospective investor. Each prospective investor should consult its own tax advisor as to the particular tax consequences to it of the acquisition, ownership, and disposition of the Notes, including the effects of applicable U.S. federal, state, and local tax laws and non-U.S. tax laws and possible changes in tax laws.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Because the Notes are denominated in the Indonesian Rupiah, a United States holder of the Notes will generally be subject to special United States federal income tax rules governing foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions, as described in the Prospectus in the last four paragraphs of "-Payments of Interest" under the "United States Holders" section. Pursuant to such rules, a United States holder should determine amounts received with respect to a Note (including principal and interest) by reference to the U.S. dollar value of the Indonesian Rupiah amount of the payment, calculated at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rate in effect on the date of payment. The U.S. dollar amount that is actually received by the United States holder may differ from the amount determined under the preceding sentence, since the U.S. dollar amount of the payment will be determined by reference to the Reference Rate as of the relevant Rate Fixing Date. Accordingly, a United States holder of the Notes may recognize United States source foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain or loss in an amount equal to such difference (in addition to any foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain or loss otherwise recognized upon the receipt of an interest payment or a sale or retirement of the Notes). The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Internal Revenue Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  could take the position, however, that the\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inter-American Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Issue of Debt -6-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 amounts received by a United States holder in respect of a Note should be equal to the U.S. dollar amount that is actually received by the United States holder. Prospective United States holders of the Notes should consult their tax advisors regarding these rules.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INTER-AMERICAN DEVELOPMENT BANK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS, the news service of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 . RNS is approved by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Conduct Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2  to act as a Primary Information Provider in the United Kingdom. Terms and conditions relating to the use and distribution of this information may apply. For further information, please contact rns@lseg.com or visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rns.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rns.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RNS may use your IP address to confirm compliance with the terms and conditions, to analyse how you engage with the information contained in this communication, and to share such analysis on an anonymised basis with others as part of our commercial services. For further information about how RNS and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  use the personal data you provide us, please see our Privacy Policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 END\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IODUNSBROUUUAAR\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 16-02-23 1744GMT\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RNS00000202