\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Indonesia c.bank\uc2  guarding against excessive rupiah falls -official\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2022\par 06:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds quote, rupiah movement and background)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Sept 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued with its "triple \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to guard against excessive falls in the rupiah exchange rate, with a focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the domestic nondeliverable forward market, an official said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Edi Susianto, head of \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's monetary management department, told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would also continue to conduct "\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  twist" in the bond market with a focus on selling short-term bonds.\par \par \uc2 His comments came after the rupiah on Wednesday fell by as much as 0.9% to 15,260 per dollar, its weakest since April, 2020.\par \par \uc2 Edi said pressure on the rupiah and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was due to market jitters after hawkish statements by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  and reports of a plan by Russia for members of OPEC+ to cut their oil output.\par \par \uc2 "Of course BI will guard (markets) with triple \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so that market mechanism is maintained and there is no wild or excessive (rupiah) depreciation," he said in a text message.\par \par \uc2 "The triple \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more focused on DNDF (domestic nondeliverable forwards) to manage market players' expectations," he said.\par \par \uc2 BI uses the term "triple \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " for its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , DNDF and bond markets.\par \par \uc2 Recently, its bond market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been done under what it called "\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  twist", in which BI sells bonds with short-term maturities and buys long-term ones.\par \par \uc2 The objective is to raise short-term yields and make the bonds more attractive for foreign investors, while also helping the government maintain relatively low borrowing costs for longer-term loans.\par \par \uc2 BI's moves in the bond market will depend on market developments, Edi said.\par \par \uc2 BI has raised interest rates twice by a total of 75 basis points since August to rein in domestic inflation and support the rupiah. (Reporting by Gayatri Suroyo Editing by Ed Davies) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-28T05:28:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220928ei9s00kwt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
