\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  gain on dollar dip; Philippine stocks slide\b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2022\par 08:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \par         * \par       Asian markets in cautious mood\par     \par \par         * \par       Philippine stocks near 2-year low\par     \par \par         * \par       South Korea's won leads gains\par     \par \par         * \par       Malaysia's ringgit lingers at over 24-year low\par     \par \par   \par     By Upasana Singh\par        Sept 27 (Reuters) - Asian emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  steadied\par on Tuesday as the dollar took a breather after notching a\par 20-year high, while Philippines shares tumbled following the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2 's warning about the country's\par economic growth.\par     India's rupee and South Korea's won\par firmed 0.4% and 0.5%, respectively, while the Thai baht\par rose 0.2%.\par     Investors' appetite for risk-sensitive Asian assets got a\par boost as the U.S. dollar index fell 0.5% to 113.35,\par pulling back from a two-decade peak of 114.58 on Monday.\par     However, the dollar has gained about 20% so far this year,\par on the back of higher interest rates, and its unrelenting rally\par has weighed heavily on the region's emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with\par most of them nursing heavy losses this year.\par     "King dollar continues to hold court within the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par universe amid the Fed's (\f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) aggressive battle\par against multi-decade high inflation," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Han Tan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief market\par analyst at Exinity Group.\par     "Further drastic declines in Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could heighten the\par prospects of more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region in\par order to shore up support for their respective \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par     The peso, which has slumped 13.5% this year and is\par the second-worst performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region, was up\par marginally, while Philippine stocks hit their lowest\par level since October 2020.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Monday flagged that the\par country's economy will grow more slowly this year than\par previously thought due to the global economic slowdown and\par tightening financial conditions.\par     Among other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , China's yuan\par weakened 0.3% and led losses.\par     Data showed that profits at the country's industrial firms\par shrank at a faster pace in January-August, as strict COVID\par restrictions and a deepening property slump weighed on domestic\par demand.\par     China's zero-COVID policy has led to lockdowns of cities and\par shut down factory \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  across the world's second-largest\par economy and Southeast Asia's biggest trading partner.\par     "We expect policy makers to take important steps in the\par coming months that would be consistent with a broad reopening\par from the spring of 2023," analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said in a\par note, adding the recovery will strengthen from the second\par quarter.\par     Meanwhile, Malaysia's ringgit fell 0.2% and\par Indonesia's rupiah shed 0.1% to hit a more-than-two-year\par low.\par     A senior official said on Monday that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par be ready with its "triple \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " in the foreign market to\par prevent any excessive fall in the rupiah, which has lost about\par 6% so far this year against the dollar.\par     Equities in Seoul were flat, while Singapore's\par benchmark index retreated 0.7%.\par     Stocks in Taipei and equities in Shanghai\par rose 0.4% and 0.8%, respectively.\par     HIGHLIGHTS:\par     ** \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai c.bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to go for another modest 25 bps hike on\par Wednesday, according to a Reuters poll\par     ** \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai c.bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  monitoring baht weakness, no big worry yet -\par FinMin\par     ** China regulators ask funds to stabilise markets before\par Communist Party Congress - sources\par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0624 GMT.\par  COUNTRY   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC          \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   INDE  STOCKS  STOCKS\par                       DAILY %  YTD %     X   DAILY   YTD %\par                                                  %  \par  Japan                  +0.35  -20.2  <.N2    -       -\par                                    2  25>           \par  China     <CNY=CFXS    -0.26  -11.1  <.SS    0.78  -15.51\par            >                       6  EC>           \par  India                  +0.37  -8.60  <.NS    0.04   -1.90\par                                       EI>           \par  Indonesi               -0.13  -5.91  <.JK   -0.49    7.77\par  a                                    SE>           \par  Malaysia               -0.17  -9.66  <.KL    0.00   -9.85\par                                       SE>           \par  Philippi               +0.08  -13.5  <.PS   -4.72  -16.26\par  nes          