he amount of interest \par                                                              payable (the "Interest Amount") \par                                                              with respect to each Calculation \par                                                              Amount on the relevant Interest \par                                                              Payment Date. \par                                                              The Interest Amount payable \par                                                              on any Interest Payment Date \par                                                              shall be a USD amount calculated \par                                                              on the relevant Rate Fixing \par                                                              Date (as defined below) as follows: \par                                                              5.100% multiplied by the Calculation \par                                                              Amount \par  \par                                                              multiplied by \par  \par                                                              the Fixed Rate Day Count Fraction \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inter-American Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Issue of Debt -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                                              divided by \par  \par                                                              the Reference Rate \par  \par                                                              (and rounding, if necessary, \par                                                              the entire resulting figure \par                                                              to the nearest two decimal places, \par                                                              with USD 0.005 being rounded \par                                                              upwards).