                                     to such Notes in, from or otherwise \par                                                              involving the UK. \par                                       (c) Indonesia:        The Notes are not and will not \par                                                              be registered with the Financial \par                                                              Services Authority previously \par                                                              known as the Capital Market \par                                                              and Financial Institutions Supervisory \par                                                              Agency (the "OJK") in Indonesia. \par                                                              As such, the Notes (including \par                                                              the distribution and dissemination \par                                                              of the Pricing Supplement, other \par                                                              written materials either through \par                                                              advertisements or other media \par                                                              authorized) are not authorized \par                                                              by the OJK for their sale by \par                                                              public offering in the Indonesian \par                                                              territory and/or to Indonesian \par                                                              entities or residents in the \par                                                              Indonesian territory in circumstances \par                                                              which constitute a public offering \par                                                              of securities under the Indonesian \par                                                              Law No. 8/1995 regarding Capital \par                                                              Markets. Likewise, the Notes \par                                                              and the Pricing Supplement have \par                                                              not been reviewed, registered \par                                                              or authorized by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central \par                                                              Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) for their \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inter-American Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Issue of Debt -5-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                                              distribution through banking \par                                                              institutions in Indonesia. As \par                                                              such, the Dealer represents \par                                                              and agrees that (a) it has not \par                                                              offered or sold and will not \par                                                              offer or sell any Notes in the \par                                                              Republic of Indonesia or to \par                                                              Indonesian nationals, corporates \par                                                              or residents including by way \par                                                              of invitation, offering or advertisement, \par                                                              and (b) it has not distributed, \par                                                              and will not distribute, the \par                                                              Prospectus, the Pricing Supplement, \par                                                              or any other offering material \par                                                              relating to the Notes in the \par                                                              Republic of Indonesia, or to \par                                                              Indonesian nationals, corporates \par                                                              or residents, in a manner which \par                                                              constitutes a public offering \par                                                              of the Notes under the laws \par                                                              and regulations of the Republic \par                                                              of Indonesia . \par                                       (d) Singapore:        In the case of the Notes being \par                                                              offered into Singapore in a \par                                                              primary or subsequent distribution, \par                                                              and solely for the purposes \par                                                              of its obligations pursuant \par                                                              to Section 309B of the Securities \par                                                              and Futures Act (Chapter 289) \par                                                              of Singapore (the "SFA"), the \par                                                              Issuer has determined, and hereby \par                                                              notifies all relevant persons \par                                                              (as defined in Section 309A \par                                                              of the SFA) that the Notes are \par                                                              "prescribed capital markets \par                                                              products" (as defined in the \par                                                              Securities and Futures (Capital \par                                                              Markets Products) Regulations \par                                                              2018 of Singapore) and Excluded \par                                                              Investment Products (as defined \par                                                              in MAS Notice SFA 04-N12: Notice \par                                                              on the Sale of Investment Products \par                                                              and MAS Notice \f28 \uc2 \f2 FAA\f28 \uc2 \f2 -N16: Notice \par                                                              on Recommendations on Investment \par                                                              Products) . \par                                       (e) General:          No action has been or will be \par                                                              taken by the Issuer that would \par                                                              permit a public offering of \par                                                              the Notes, or possession or \par                                                              distribution of any offering \par                                                              material relating to the Notes \par                                                              in any jurisdiction where action \par                                                              for that purpose is required. \par                                                              Accordingly, the Dealer agrees \par                                                              that it will observe all applicable \par                                                              provisions of law in each jurisdiction \par                                                              in or from which it may offer \par                                                              or sell Notes or distribute \par                                                              any offering material. \par  \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additional Information Regarding the Notes \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    1.         Matters relating to UK MiFIR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank does not fall under the scope of application of the UK MiFIR regime. Consequently, the Bank does not qualify as an "investment firm", "manufacturer" or "distributor" for the purposes of UK MiFIR.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 UK MiFIR product governance / Retail investors, professional investors and ECPs target market - Solely for the purposes of the UK manufacturer's product approval process, the target market assessment in respect of the Notes has led to the conclusion that: (i) the target market for the Notes is retail clients, as defined in point (8) of Article 2 of Regulation (EU) No 2017/565 as it forms part of UK domestic law by virtue of the EUWA, eligible counterparties, as defined in COBS, and professional clients, as defined in UK MiFIR; and (ii) all channels for distribution of the Notes are appropriate . Any person subsequently offering, selling or recommending the Notes (a "distributor") should take into consideration the UK manufacturer's target market assessment; however, a distributor subject to the UK MiFIR Product Governance Rules is responsible for undertaking its own target market assessment in respect of the Notes (by either adopting or refining the UK manufacturer's target market assessment) and determining appropriate distribution channels.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the purposes of this provision, (i) the expression "UK manufacturer" means the Dealer, (ii) the expression "COBS" means the \f28 \uc2 \f2 FCA\f28 \uc2 \f2  Handbook Conduct of Business Sourcebook, (iii) the expression "UK MiFIR" means Regulation (EU) No 600/2014 as it forms part of UK domestic law by virtue of the EUWA and (iv) the expression "UK MiFIR Product Governance Rules" means the \f28 \uc2 \f2 FCA\f28 \uc2 \f2  Handbook Product \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Product Governance Sourcebook. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.         Additional Investment Considerations: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Notes offered by this Pricing Supplement are complex financial instruments and may not be suitable for certain investors. Investors intending to purchase the Notes should consult with their tax and financial advisors to ensure that the intended purchase meets the investment objective before making such purchase.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are various risks associated with the Notes including, but not limited to, exchange rate risk, price risk and liquidity risk. Investors should consult with their own financial, legal and accounting advisors about the risks associated with an investment in these Notes, the appropriate tools to analyze that investment, and the suitability of the investment in each investor's particular circumstances. Holders of the Notes should also consult with their professional tax advisors regarding tax laws applicable to them.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment of each Interest Amount and the Redemption Amount will be based on the Reference Rate, which is a measure of the rate of exchange between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates are volatile and will affect the holder's return. In addition, the government of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can from time to time \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. These \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or other governmental actions could adversely affect the value of the Notes, as well as the yield (in USD terms) on the Notes and the amount payable at maturity or upon acceleration. Even in the absence of governmental action directly affecting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, political or economic developments in Indonesia or elsewhere could lead to significant and sudden changes in the exchange rate between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian Rupiah is an emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be subject to particularly substantial volatility, as well as to government actions including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls, devaluations and other matters which could materially and adversely affect the value of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The methodologies for determining the Reference Rate may result in a Redemption Amount (or Early Redemption Amount, as the case may be) of the Notes, or an Interest Amount on the Notes, being significantly less than anticipated or less than what an alternative methodology for determining the IDR-USD exchange rate would yield. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.         United Stated Federal Income Tax Matters: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Inter-American Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Issue of Debt -6-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following supplements the discussion under the "Tax Matters" section of the Prospectus regarding the U.S. federal income tax treatment of the Notes, and is subject to the limitations and exceptions set forth therein. Any tax disclosure in the Prospectus or this Pricing Supplement is of a general nature only, is not exhaustive of all possible tax considerations and is not intended to be, and should not be construed to be, legal, business or tax advice to any particular prospective investor. Each prospective investor should consult its own tax advisor as to the particular tax consequences to it of the acquisition, ownership, and disposition of the Notes, including the effects of applicable U.S. federal, state, and local tax laws and non-U.S. tax laws and possible changes in tax laws.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Because the Notes should be treated as issued in a qualified reopening within the meaning of \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Regulations Section 1.1275-2(k)(3), the issue price of the Notes for U.S. federal income tax purposes should be the same as the issue price of the Series 815 Tranche 1 Notes. Accordingly, the Notes should not be treated as issued with original issue discount, or OID, for U.S. federal income tax purposes, even though the initial discount on the Notes exceeds the de minimis threshold (for more information on OID, see the Prospectus at "- Original Issue Discount" under the "United States Holders" section). A United States holder of the Notes should instead be subject to the market discount rules (described in the Prospectus at "- Market Discount" under the "United States Holders" section) with respect to the excess of the principal amount of the Notes over the price at which the holder purchases the Notes (excluding amounts paid in respect of accrued interest).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Because the Notes are denominated in the Indonesian Rupiah, a United States holder of the Notes will generally be subject to special United States federal income tax rules governing foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions, as described in the Prospectus in the last four paragraphs of "-Payments of Interest" under the "United States Holders" section. Pursuant to such rules, a United States holder should determine amounts received with respect to a Note (including principal and interest) by reference to the U.S. dollar value of the Indonesian Rupiah amount of the payment, calculated at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rate in effect on the date of payment. The U.S. dollar amount that is actually received by the United States holder may differ from the amount determined under the preceding sentence, since the U.S. dollar amount of the payment will be determined by reference to the Reference Rate as of the relevant Rate Fixing Date. Accordingly, a United States holder of the Notes may recognize United States source foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain or loss in an amount equal to such difference (in addition to any foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain or loss otherwise recognized upon the receipt of an interest payment or a sale or retirement of the Notes). The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Internal Revenue Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  could take the position, however, that the amounts received by a United States holder in respect of a Note should be equal to the U.S. dollar amount that is actually received by the United States holder. Prospective United States holders of the Notes should consult their tax advisors regarding these rules.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INTER-AMERICAN DEVELOPMENT BANK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS, the news service of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2 . RNS is approved by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Conduct Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2  to act as a Primary Information Provider in the United Kingdom. Terms and conditions relating to the use and distribution of this information may apply. For further information, please contact rns@lseg.com or visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rns.com"}