\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves rise to $137.1 bln in June\b0\par\par\uc2 115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2021\par 05:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, July 7 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose by some $700 million in June to $137.1 billion, equivalent to 9.2 months of imports, boosted by proceeds from a government issuance of U.S. dollar-denominated Islamic bonds, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The rise came despite the rupiah coming under pressure in June amid global market volatility after the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  turned hawkish on stimulus withdrawal plans. \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pledged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to smooth any volatility in the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Gayatri Suroyo Editing by Ed Davies) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-7-7T04:10:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210707eh7700bf9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
