\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia cbank gov commits to loose policy, says  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves enough for stability\b0\par\par\uc2 426 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 06:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at record high at end-Feb\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah down as much as 0.65% on Wed (Rewrites to add further remarks by c.bank governor)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, March 31 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor reaffirmed a commitment to keep policy loose to support an economic recovery and said it has enough \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to guard the rupiah exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 In a pre-recorded remarks for a \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2 ' seminar on Wednesday, Governor \uc2 Perry Warjiyo\uc2  said \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 "will not hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 " to guard the rupiah against external shock, using its so-called "triple \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in the spot, domestic non-deliverable forward and bond markets.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has been falling in the past month against the U.S. dollar on the back of capital outflows triggered by rising U.S. treasury yields. It dropped by as much as 0.65% on Wednesday to 14,564 per dollar, the weakest since Nov. 3.\par \par \uc2 "Our exchange rate basically and mostly will be determined by market mechanism, supply-demand, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ensures the market mechanism is continuing to be consistent with the fundamentals," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We provide commitment to ensure rupiah will be stable despite increasing uncertainty in the global market," he added. "The rupiah exchange rate is important to support economic recovery."\par \par \uc2 He said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which hit a record high of $138.8 billion at end February, were "more than ample" to ensure external stability.\par \par \uc2 Warjiyo reiterated that all of the bank's tools, including monetary, macroprudential and payment system policies, were currently geared towards accelerating an economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 BI has cut interest rates by a cumulative 150 basis points and pumped more than $50 billion into the financial system to help Southeast Asia's largest economy weather the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The economy was on track to grow by 4.3% to 5.3% this year and 5.2% next year, after GDP contracted 2.07% last year, he said.\par \par \uc2 The governor's remarks came a day after a sovereign bond auction attracted the lowest bids since April amid weak foreign demand.\par \par \uc2 Warjiyo reiterated in the seminar that BI has an outstanding agreement with the government to become a standby buyer in auctions until end-2022 and that its special arrangement of direct fiscal deficit financing was a one-off policy in 2020 that will not be repeated. (Reporting by Gayatri Suroyo and Tabita Diela; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-31T05:40:25.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210331eh3v00jzh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
