\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Indonesia leads Asia stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  higher as c.bank holds fire\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 08:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting later on Thursday\par     * Malaysia govt announces $4.87 bln stimulus \par     * Indonesia's rupiah up 0.4%, stocks over 1%\par \par     March 18 (Reuters) - Indonesia led Asia's emerging stocks\par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets higher on Thursday as the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as expected left its key policy rate unchanged following\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's pledge to keep interest rates near\par zero.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BI) \f28 \uc2 \f2 said it will continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the market to keep the rupiah stable as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  comes under\par pressure from capital outflows.\par     Meanwhile, Philippines and Singapore stocks\par rose around 1% after the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would not\par wind back stimulus despite a stronger U.S. economic outlook and\par an expected surge in inflation.\par     The yields on benchmark 10-year Treasury note\par hit a 13-month high, helping the dollar index rise 0.2%\par and limiting gains in Asia's risk-sensitive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The index had slumped 0.6% on Wednesday after the Fed's\par remarks on economic growth, with DBS analysts attributing the\par sell-off to profit-taking on gains made in the run up to the\par policy meeting.\par     Indonesian stocks were up 1.2% after BI's decision.\par Analysts were expecting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to keep its 7-day\par reverse repurchase rate unchanged at a record low\par of 3.50% as rising U.S. yields puts pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     BI has cut rates by 150 basis points over six cuts since the\par pandemic started.\par     Asia's higher-yielding bonds were also moving in tight\par ranges following the Fed decision. U.S. bond yields have been\par rising on expectations that a faster economic recovery could\par fuel inflation and prompt the Fed to start unwinding ultra-loose\par monetary policy.\par     Citi analysts said a growing U.S. economy and higher\par inflation might "keep (the) U.S. curve steep and prevent lasting\par relief for Asia fixed income."   \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will hold its policy meeting later on\par Thursday, with interest rates expected to be left unchanged.\par \par     The local dollar was flat through the day, and\par stocks closed nearly half a percent higher.\par     The local dollar, which has strengthened over 6% in the\par year, has become a source of concern for the export-reliant\par economy that saw strong growth last year from demand for its\par technology products.\par     Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor recently said the island may\par be labelled a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manipulator by the United States, having\par met Washington's three main criteria for such a decision.\par \par     Last week, data showed a big spike in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par spending last year.\par     In Malaysia, stocks and the ringgit were up\par less than half a percent. The government unveiled a fresh round\par of stimulus on Wednesday, totalling 20 billion ringgit ($4.87\par billion).\par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS: \par     ** Indonesian 10-year benchmark yields are down 0.6 basis\par points at 6.751%\par     ** Malaysia to sell 4.5 bln ringgit government bonds\par \par     ** \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jardine Matheson Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Genting\par Singapore Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  led gains in Singapore\par     \par   Asia stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at   0740 GMT\par  COUNTRY      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2      INDEX    STOCKS   STOCKS\par                           DAILY %  YTD %           DAILY %  YTD %\par  Japan                    -0.32    -5.44           1.01     10.10\par  China                    +0.06    +0.42           0.51     -0.29\par  India                    -0.04    +0.68           0.37     5.68\par  Indonesia                +0.38    -2.30           1.18     6.22\par  Malaysia                 +0.27    -2.14           0.44     0.30\par  Philippines              -0.27    -1.42           0.97     -7.13\par  S.Korea                  +0.58    -3.34           0.61     6.70\par  Singapore                -0.17    -1.59           0.81     10.24\par  Taiwan                   -0.04    +0.60           0.44     10.56\par  Thailand                 +0.03    -2.60           0.55     8.70\par  ($1 = 4.1050 ringgit)\par \par  (Reporting by Nikhil Kurian Nainan and Nikhil Subba in\par Bengaluru; Editing by Arun Koyyur)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-18T08:49:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210318eh3i010ll\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
