\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank\uc2  says ready for market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to stabilise rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 04:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, March 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to keep the rupiah steady by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in financial markets whenever necessary, a \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 spokesman said on Friday, after a gradual fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following rising U.S. treasury yields.\par \par \uc2 "BI is always in the market for triple \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , through spot, DNDF (domestic NDF) and also purchasing bonds if necessary," spokesman Erwin Haryono said, adding that many other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also fell due to the movements of U.S. yields.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah traded at 14,300 per dollar at 0325 GMT, down 0.3% from a day earlier. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dropped more than 1% in slightly over a week. (Reporting by Tabita Diela; Writing by Gayatri Suroyo Editing by Ed Davies) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-5T04:32:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210305eh3500mop\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
