\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Indonesia stocks trip as c.bank seen holding rates\b0\par\par\uc2 670 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2020\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: Foreign flows into Asian stocks \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3lKhL5I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3lKhL5I}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  expected to hold interest rates - Reuters poll\par     * Experts call for BI to remain independent\par     * Singapore stocks snap 5-day losing run\par \par     By Shashwat Awasthi\par     Sept 15 (Reuters) - Indonesia stocks pulled back on Tuesday after a more than 5% surge over\par the last two sessions as a Reuters poll of analysts predicted the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would\par stand pat on interest rates in favour of supporting an under-pressure rupiah.\par     Upbeat Chinese data supported other emerging Asian share markets at the start of a week that\par also sees meetings of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Jakarta's stock market, however, was the biggest decliner ahead of Thursday's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting and after Indonesia reported a steeper-than-expected drop in imports and\par exports for August.\par     Brokerage Samuel Sekuritas in a note to clients also cited profit-taking for the weakness in\par Indonesian equities.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BI) \f28 \uc2 \f2 has had to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stabilize the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  multiple times this month\par as foreign investors worry about the bank's independence, the country's debt and growth\par prospects.\par     The rupiah firmed as much as 0.2% and stocks came off session lows, however, after\par experts insisted BI must remain independent while calling for an expansion of the bank's mandate\par before a parliamentary committee.\par     Other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also rose against a subdued U.S. dollar.\par     The dollar has been sold heavily against its developed world counterparts in the past three\par months, and data on speculative positions show global investors are also net "long" on emerging\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the greenback, following the Fed's rejigging of its policy framework to spur\par growth and inflation.\par     The emerging positions, however, are far less extended, reflecting the risks investors see\par around growth and the heavy load of coronavirus cases across a number of major developing\par markets.\par     \par     \par     Singapore stocks advanced 0.5%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jeffrey Halley\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a strategist with trading platform\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 OANDA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , attributed the move to a sign of confidence in the local market after China's Tencent\par  chose the city-state as its Asia hub.\par     In the Philippines, which reported record coronavirus deaths for the second time in three\par days on Monday, shares recouped earlier losses to gain 0.4%.\par     "While the overall tone remains cautious over fears of COVID-19 cases resurgence due to\par gradual easing of physical distancing protocols, market's risk appetite seems to have picked\par up," said Jennifer Lomboy, a fund manager at First Metro Asset Management.\par     "With the strong run of some defensive names, local players were seen slowly shifting to\par cyclicals as market confidence on economic recovery builds up."\par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS\par     \par     ** Indonesian 3-year benchmark yields are up 27.9 basis points at 4.971%\par     ** Top losers on the Jakarta stock index include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Destinasi Tirta Nusantara\f28 \uc2 \f2  down\par 6.99%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asuransi Bintang\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 6.94% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tridomain Performance Materials\f28 \uc2 \f2  down\par 6.94%\par     ** In the Philippines, top index gainers are \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alliance Global\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 2.95%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bloomberry\par Resorts\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 2.79% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Metropolitan Bank and Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 2.72%\par         \par     \par     Asia stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 0656 GMT                                    \par    COUNTRY      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DAILY %     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  YTD %     INDEX   STOCKS DAILY %  STOCKS YTD %\par     Japan                    +0.05         +2.78                   -0.44          -0.85\par     China                    +0.34         +2.62                    0.53           8.07\par     India                    -0.03         -2.88                    0.44          -5.57\par   Indonesia                  +0.20         -6.41                   -0.93          -18.82\par   Malaysia                   +0.31         -0.99                    0.51          -4.38\par  Philippines                 -0.10         +4.48                    0.35          -22.99\par    S.Korea                   +0.38         -1.92                    0.65          11.19\par   Singapore                  +0.26         -1.19                    0.45          -22.63\par    Taiwan                    +0.90         +3.02                    0.45           7.07\par   Thailand                   +0.32         -4.20                    0.49          -19.07\par  \par     \par  (Reporting by Shashwat Awasthi and Anushka Trivedi in Bengaluru; Editing by Saumyadeb\par Chakrabarty)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-9-15T08:40:47.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200915eg9f016o5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
