\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Indonesian stocks lag Asian peers as c.bank seen holding rates this week\b0\par\par\uc2 643 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2020\par 08:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://tmsnrt.rs/2egbfVh}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * Graphic: Foreign flows into Asian stocks \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3lKhL5I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3lKhL5I}}}\uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  expected to hold interest rates - Reuters poll\par     * Singapore shares snap 5-day losing run\par \par     By Shashwat Awasthi\par     Sept 15 (Reuters) - Indonesia's stocks eased on Tuesday after two days of gains as investors\par braced for a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate decision later this week, underperforming other emerging Asian\par markets supported by upbeat Chinese data.\par     Jakarta's stock market was the biggest daily loser, falling 1.3% ahead of Thursday's\par monetary policy meeting, with analysts in a Reuters poll betting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would hold off\par further lowering interest rates to avoid putting additional pressure on the rupiah.\par     The rupiah firmed slightly on the day, while Taiwan's dollar led gains among\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against a subdued U.S. dollar.\par     The yuan hit a 16-month high on data showing China's industrial output\par accelerated the most in eight months in August and retail sales grew for the first time this\par year.\par     The data supported markets in Malaysia, South Korea and Thailand at\par the start of a full week, which will also see meetings from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of\par Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Philippine shares fell after the country reported a record number of COVID-19 deaths\par for the second time in three days, calling into question its decision to relax social distancing\par rules. But the shares later recouped losses to trade higher on the day.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has had to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  multiple times this month as\par foreign investors worried about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's independence, rising coronavirus cases, debt\par and economic growth.\par     Indonesia also reported on Tuesday a worse-than-expected contraction of imports and exports\par in August, with analysts at ING saying that slowing economic activity was capping demand for\par capital goods and raw materials.\par     The dollar has been sold heavily against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in recent months and data on\par speculative positions show global investors are net "long" emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the\par greenback after the Fed said it would target average inflation, giving it more flexibility to\par spur growth..\par \par     In Singapore, the FTSE Strait Times Index advanced 0.6%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jeffrey Halley\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a strategist\par with trading platform \f28 \uc2 \f2 OANDA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , attributed the move to sentiment around China's Tencent\par choosing the city-state as its Asia hub.\par     "With unemployment at record highs by Singapore standards, this will be seen as a welcome\par shot of confidence in the local market," he said.  \par     \par     HIGHLIGHTS\par     \par     ** Indonesian 3-year benchmark yields are up 27.9 basis points at 4.971%\par     ** Top losers on the Jakarta stock index include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Destinasi Tirta Nusantara\f28 \uc2 \f2  down\par 6.99%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Intan Baruprana Finance\f28 \uc2 \f2  down 6.92% and Sunson Textile Manufacturer\par down 6.87%\par     ** Top gainers on the Singapore STI include \f28 \uc2 \f2 Genting Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 2.24%, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mapletree\par Industrial Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  up 2.22% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai Beverage\f28 \uc2 \f2  up \u8203\'20\'0B1.68%\par     \par     \par    Asia stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 0409 GMT                                    \par    COUNTRY      \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RIC    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  DAILY %    \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  YTD %     INDEX    STOCKS DAILY %  STOCKS YTD %\par     Japan                    +0.04        +2.77                   -0.63          -1.04\par     China                    +0.32        +2.59                    0.28           7.80\par     India                    +0.00        -2.85                    0.47          -5.55\par   Indonesia                  +0.13        -6.47                   -1.14          -19.00\par   Malaysia                   +0.27        -1.04                    0.68          -4.23\par  Philippines                 +0.04        +4.63                   -0.26          -23.47\par    S.Korea                   +0.24        -2.06                    0.48          11.01\par   Singapore                  +0.24        -1.22                    0.64          -22.48\par    Taiwan                    +0.88        +3.00                    0.35           6.97\par   Thailand                   +0.35        -4.17                    0.27          -19.24\par             \par \par     \par  (Reporting by Shashwat Awasthi in Bengaluru; Editing by Patrick Graham and Ana Nicolaci da\par Costa)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-9-15T07:20:19.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200915eg9f00vsh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
