\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  defends rupiah as doubts rise over c.bank independence\b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2020\par 06:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah falls on worry over BI independence, debt monetisation               \par \par \uc2 * Parliament considers proposal giving govt more authority over BI (Adds comments, market movement)               \par \par \uc2 By Gayatri Suroyo and Fransiska Nangoy               \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Sept 2 (Reuters) - \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth volatility in the rupiah on Wednesday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under pressure on worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence following a proposal to give the government more authority in monetary policy decisions.               \par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell 1.6% by 0350 GMT on Wednesday to trade at 14,800 a dollar, the weakest since Aug. 18.               \par \par \uc2 Nanang Hendarsah, \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's (BI) head of monetary management, told Reuters it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot interbank market to smooth volatility, but declined to comment on other topics.               \par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joko Widodo\uc2  pledged on Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain independent after a panel of experts advising parliament recommended ministers be given voting rights at policy meetings and for BI's mandate to be widened to include economic growth and employment.               \par \par \uc2 The proposals are for a bill for the second revision of the 1999 \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  act.               \par \par \uc2 The recommendations also included allowing BI to buy government bonds in the primary market and purchase zero-interest bonds under certain economic conditions, \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently doing only in response to the pandemic.               \par \par \uc2 BI has pledged to buy $28 billion of government bonds while relinquishing interest payments, as part of a $40 billion fiscal financing deal with the government to fight the health crisis in 2020.               \par \par \uc2 Widodo told foreign correspondents the so-called "burden-sharing" scheme would continue to 2021, but it was unlikely to be extended beyond that timeframe if economic growth recovers to 4.5%-5.5% by next year. The government expects a small contraction or flat growth this year due to the pandemic.               \par \par \uc2 "Investors are worried about the news on the extension of burden sharing with BI to 2022 and concerned about BI's independence," a Jakarta-based \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader told Reuters.               \par \par \uc2 Citibank wrote in a research note the bill and concerns over unconventional monetary policy "adds to medium term weakening expectations for IDR".               \par \par \uc2 Analysts at ING said the bill "would undermine BI's independence and could open the door to successive rounds of debt monetisation, something that would rattle investor confidence and exert additional depreciation pressure on the IDR."               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-9-2T05:59:06.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200902eg9200jd9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
