\par\par \b \uc2 SE Asia Stocks-Philippines falls as imports dive, Indonesia virus cases surge\b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2020\par 06:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Indonesia headed for biggest daily drop since May 4\par     * Philippines posts record drop in April imports\par     * Thailand, Singapore both up\par \par     By Arundhati Dutta\par     June 10 (Reuters) - Philippine stocks plunged more than 3%\par on Wednesday as April trade data pointed to a plunge in economic\par activity, while the Indonesian market dropped after a surge in\par daily coronavirus cases.\par     The Philippines' April imports plunged by a record 65%, and\par exports by 51%, reducing the trade deficit to the lowest in five\par years but pointing to a collapse in domestic economic output.\par \par     Leading losses in South-east Asia, the Philippines benchmark\par index dropped as much as 3.5%. Blue chip conglomerates \f28 \uc2 \f2 SM\par Investments Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ayala Land Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell 4.7%\par and 3.2%, respectively. \par     The Indonesian index slipped by up to 2.5%, and was\par headed for its biggest daily drop in a month. Financials\par accounted around half the benchmark's losses, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Bank\par Central Asia Tbk\f28 \uc2 \f2  skidding as much as 3.2%. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Wednesday it was\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to stabilise the rupiah.\par \par     "There are some concerns that Indonesia could face a second\par wave in number of cases," said  Andry E. Taneli, a portfolio\par manager at Ciptadana Asset Management in Jakarta. \par     The country reported 1,043 new coronavirus infections on\par Tuesday, its biggest daily rise yet.\par     On the upside, Thai stocks added up to 0.9% in early\par trade, with consumer discretionary and utilities sectors leading\par the gains. \par     Singaporean equities edged higher, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 United\par Overseas Bank Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2  UOBH.SI> up 1%. \par     \par For Asian Companies click;  \par \par SOUTHEAST ASIAN STOCK MARKETS AS AT 0404 GMT\par     \par   STOCK MARKETS                                        \par   Change on the                                        \par  day                                          \par   Market           Current       Previous     Pct Move\par                                  close        \par   Singapore        2796.82       2794.17      0.09\par   Bangkok          1414.01       1408.37      0.40\par   Manila           6365.75       6583.84      -3.31\par   Jakarta          4907.403      5035.055     -2.54\par   Kuala Lumpur     1574.56       1575.16      -0.04\par  Ho Chi Minh       895.1         899.43       -0.48\par                                               \par   Change so far                               \par  in 2020                                      \par   Market           Current       End 2019     Pct Move\par   Singapore        2796.82       3222.83      -13.22\par   Bangkok          1414.01       1579.84      -10.50\par   Manila           6365.75       7,815.26     -18.55\par   Jakarta          4907.403      6,299.54     -22.10\par   Kuala Lumpur     1574.56       1588.76      -0.89\par   Ho Chi Minh      895.1         960.99       -6.86\par  \par \par  (Reporting by Arundhati Dutta; Editing by Rashmi Aich)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-6-10T05:47:46.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200610eg6a00hwh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
