\par\par \b \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt\b0\par\par\uc2 4,969 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2020\par 08:00\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2020 \par \par \uc2 TIDM42BI\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 8762K\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 27 April 2020\par \par \uc2 PRICING SUPPLEMENT\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 Global Debt Program\par \par \uc2 Series No.: 747\par \par \uc2 IDR 55,000,000,000 6.600 percent Notes due April 24, 2023 (the "Notes")\par \par \uc2 payable in United States Dollars\par \par \uc2 Issue Price: 100.026 percent\par \par \uc2 Application has been made for the Notes to be admitted to the Official List of the \uc2 Financial Conduct Authority\uc2  and to trading on the \uc2 London Stock Exchange plc\uc2 's Regulated Market\par \par \uc2 J.P. Morgan\par \par \uc2 The date of this Pricing Supplement is as of April 21, 2020\par \par \uc2 Terms used herein shall be deemed to be defined as such for the purposes of the Terms and Conditions (the "Conditions") set forth in the Prospectus dated January 8, 2001 (the "Prospectus") (which for the avoidance of doubt does not constitute a prospectus for the purposes of Part VI of the United Kingdom Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 or a base prospectus for the purposes of Regulation (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) 2017/1129). This Pricing Supplement must be read in conjunction with the Prospectus. This document is issued to give details of an issue by the \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  (the "Bank") under its Global Debt Program and to provide information supplemental to the Prospectus. Complete information in respect of the Bank and this offer of the Notes is only available on the basis of the combination of this Pricing Supplement and the Prospectus.\par \par \uc2 MiFID II product governance / Retail investors, professional investors and ECPs target market - See "General Information-Additional Information Regarding the Notes-Matters relating to MiFID II" below.\par \par \uc2 Terms and Conditions\par \par \uc2 The following items under this heading "Terms and Conditions" are the particular terms which relate to the issue the subject of this Pricing Supplement. These are the only terms which form part of the form of Notes for such issue. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par       1.    Series No.:                      747 \par       2.    Aggregate Principal Amount:      IDR 55,000,000,000 \par       3.    Issue Price:                          IDR 55,014,300,000 which amount \par                                                    represents 100.026 percent of \par                                                   the Aggregate Principal Amount. \par                                                   The Issue Price will be payable \par                                               in USD in the amount of USD 3,391,757.09 \par                                                   at the agreed rate of 16,220 IDR \par                                                             per one USD. \par       4.    Issue Date:                      April 24, 2020 \par       5.    Form of Notes \par              (Condition 1(a)):                Registered only, as further provided \par                                               in paragraph 9(c) of "Other Relevant \par                                               Terms" below. \par       6.    Authorized Denomination(s) \par               (Condition 1(b)):               IDR 10,000,000 and integral multiples \par                                               thereof \par       7.    Specified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par              (Condition 1(d)):                The lawful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Republic \par                                               of Indonesia ("Indonesian Rupiah" \par                                               or "IDR"), provided that all payments \par                                               in respect of the Notes will be \par                                               made in United States Dollars \par                                               ("U.S.$" or "USD") \par       8.    Specified Principal Payment \par              \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par              (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)):      USD \par       9.    Specified Interest Payment \par              \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          USD \par              (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)): \par       10.   Maturity Date \par              (Condition 6(a); Fixed            April 24, 2023 \par              Interest Rate): \par       11.   Interest Basis \par              (Condition 5):                   Fixed Interest Rate (Condition \par                                               5(I)) \par       12.   Interest Commencement Date \par              (Condition 5(III)):               April 24, 2020 \par       13.   Fixed Interest Rate (Condition   Condition 5(I) as amended and \par              5(I)):                           supplemented below, shall apply \par                                               to the Notes. The bases of the \par                                               Calculation of the Interest Amount, \par                                               Interest Payment Dates and default \par                                               interest are as set out below. \par  \par               (a) Interest Rate:              6.600 percent per annum \par             (b) Business Day Convention:     Following Business Day Convention \par             (c) Fixed Rate Interest \par              Payment Date(s):                  Annually on each April 24, commencing \par                                                on April 24, 2021 and ending on, \par                                                and including, the Maturity Date. \par                                                Each Interest Payment Date is \par                                                subject to adjustment in accordance \par                                                with the Following Business Day \par                                                Convention with no adjustment \par                                                to the amount of interest otherwise \par                                                calculated. \par             (d) Interest Period:             Each period from and including \par                                               each Interest Payment Date to \par                                               but excluding the next following \par                                               Interest Payment Date, provided \par                                               that the initial Interest Period \par                                               will commence on and include the \par                                               Interest Commencement Date, and \par                                               the final Interest Period will \par                                               end on but exclude the Maturity \par                                               Date. \par                                               For the purposes of the calculation \par                                               of the Interest Amount payable \par                                               for any Interest Period, there \par                                               shall be no adjustment pursuant \par                                               to the Business Day Convention \par                                               specified above. \par             (e) Fixed Rate Day Count \par              Fraction(s):                     Actual/Actual ICMA \par             (f) Calculation of Interest      As soon as practicable and in \par              Amount:                          accordance with the procedure \par                                               specified herein, the Calculation \par                                               Agent will determine the IDR Rate \par                                               (as defined below) and calculate \par                                               the amount of interest payable \par                                               (the "Interest Amount") with respect \par                                               to each minimum Authorized Denomination \par                                               for the relevant Interest Period. \par                                               The Interest Amount with respect \par                                               to any Interest Period shall be \par                                               a USD amount calculated on the \par                                               relevant Rate Fixing Date (as \par                                               defined below) as follows: \par                                               6.600% times the minimum Authorized \par                                               Denomination \par  \par                                               times \par  \par                                               the Fixed Rate Day Count Fraction \par  \par                                               divided by \par  \par                                               the IDR Rate \par  \par                                               (and rounding, if necessary, the \par                                               entire resulting figure to the \par                                               nearest two decimal places, with \par                                               USD 0.005 being rounded upwards). \par  \par                                               The "IDR Rate" means the rate \par                                               determined by the Calculation \par                                               Agent that is equal to the USD/IDR \par                                               weighted average spot rate in \par                                               the interbank market, based on \par                                               traded USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                               transactions during a specified \par                                               time period which are captured \par                                               on a real time basis, expressed \par                                               as the amount of IDR per one USD, \par                                               for settlement in two Fixing Business \par                                               Days, as published by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                               as the "Jakarta Interbank Spot \par                                               Dollar Rate USD - IDR", which \par                                               appears on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website \par                                               (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), or as published \par                                               on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2  Screen JISDOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                               Page (or any replacement page \par                                               or replacement service as may \par                                               be implemented for the purposes \par                                               of displaying the USD/IDR weighted \par                                               average spot rate), or as otherwise \par                                               made available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                               (or its successor as administrator), \par                                               at approximately 10:00 a.m., Jakarta \par                                               time, on the Rate Fixing Date \par                                               . Fallback Provisions apply as \par                                               set out below. \par                                              The "Rate Fixing Date" means the \par                                               date that is five (5) Fixing Business \par                                               Days prior to the applicable Fixed \par                                               Rate Interest Payment Date or \par                                               Maturity Date, as the case may \par                                               be. The Rate Fixing Date shall \par                                               be subject to adjustment as follows: \par                                               if the scheduled date of the Rate \par                                               Fixing Date is not a Relevant \par                                               Business Day, then the Rate Fixing \par                                               Date will be the first preceding \par                                               day that is a Relevant Business \par                                               Day. \par                                               "Fixing Business Day" means a \par                                               day (other than a Saturday or \par                                               a Sunday) on which banks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                               exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets are open for \par                                               business in Jakarta. \par                                              "Fallback Provisions": Should \par                                               no USD/IDR weighted average spot \par                                               rate appear on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                               website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ) as the \par                                               "Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar \par                                               Rate USD - IDR", or on Thomson \par                                               Reuters Screen JISDOR Page (or \par                                               on such replacement page or replacement \par                                               service as described above), or \par                                               be otherwise made available by \par                                               \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its successor \par                                               as administrator), on the Rate \par                                               Fixing Date, then the IDR Rate \par                                               for such Rate Fixing Date shall \par                                               be determined by the Calculation \par                                               Agent by requesting quotations \par                                               for the mid USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                               exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate from five banks \par                                               active in the USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                               and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets as \par                                               selected by the Calculation Agent \par                                               (such banks, the "Reference Banks") \par                                               either (i) at or about 10:00 a.m. \par                                               Jakarta time on the first day \par                                               (other than a Saturday or a Sunday) \par                                               following the Rate Fixing Date, \par                                               if such day is a Relevant Business \par                                               Day or (ii) at or about 10:00 \par                                               a.m. Jakarta time on the Rate \par                                               Fixing Date, if the first day \par                                               (other than a Saturday or a Sunday) \par                                               following the Rate Fixing Date \par                                               is not a Relevant Business Day. \par                                              If five or four quotations are \par                                               provided by Reference Banks as \par                                               requested, the IDR Rate shall \par                                               be the arithmetic mean (rounded \par                                               to the nearest whole IDR, with \par                                               IDR 0.5 being rounded upwards) \par                                               of the remaining three or two \par                                               such quotations (expressed as \par                                               the number of IDR per one USD), \par                                               as the case may be, after disregarding \par                                               the highest quotation and the \par                                               lowest quotation; provided, that \par                                               if two or more such quotations \par                                               are the highest such quotations, \par                                               then only one of such quotations \par                                               shall be disregarded; and provided \par                                               further, that if two or more such \par                                               quotations are the lowest such \par                                               quotations, then only one of such \par                                               lowest quotations shall be disregarded. \par                                               If only three or two quotations \par                                               are provided as requested, the \par                                               IDR Rate shall be the arithmetic \par                                               mean (rounded to the nearest whole \par                                               IDR, with IDR 0.5 being rounded \par                                               upwards) of such quotations (expressed \par                                               as the number of IDR per one USD). \par                                               If only one or no quotations are \par                                               provided as requested, or if the \par                                               Calculation Agent determines in \par                                               its sole discretion that no suitable \par                                               Reference Banks active in the \par                                               USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                               markets will provide quotations, \par                                               the Calculation Agent shall be \par                                               entitled to calculate the IDR \par                                               Rate acting in good faith in a \par                                               commercially reasonable manner, \par                                               having taken into account relevant \par                                               market practice, by reference \par                                               to such additional sources as \par                                               it deems appropriate; and in such \par                                               case the Calculation Agent shall \par                                               notify the Bank and the Global \par                                               Agent as soon as reasonably practicable \par                                               that the IDR Rate is to be so \par                                               determined. \par             (g) Calculation Agent:           See "8. Identity of Calculation \par                                               Agent" under "Other Relevant Terms" \par             (h) Notification:                If the Interest Amount payable \par                                               on any Fixed Rate Interest Payment \par                                               Date or the Redemption Amount, \par                                               as the case may be, is calculated \par                                               in any manner other than by utilizing \par                                               the USD/IDR reference rate that \par                                               appears on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website \par                                               (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), or on Thomson \par                                               Reuters Screen JISDOR Page ( or \par                                               on such replacement page as described \par                                               above ), or as otherwise made \par                                               available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or \par                                               its successor as administrator), \par                                               the Global Agent on behalf of \par                                               the Bank shall give notice as \par                                               soon as reasonably practicable \par                                               to the Noteholders in accordance \par                                               with Condition 14 (Notices). \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt -3-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par       14.   Relevant Financial Center:       New York, London and Jakarta \par       15.   Relevant Business Day:           New York, London and Jakarta \par       16.   Redemption Amount (Condition \par              6(a)):                            The Redemption Amount with respect \par                                                to each minimum Authorized Denomination \par                                                will be a USD amount calculated \par                                                by the Calculation Agent as of \par                                                the Rate Fixing Date with respect \par                                                to the Maturity Date as follows: \par  \par                                                minimum Authorized Denomination \par  \par                                             