\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves drop by some $9 bln amid capital outflows\b0\par\par\uc2 462 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 April 2020\par 14:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Drop in reserves in March the biggest since Sept. 2011\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah slides 14% against U.S. dollar in the month\par \par \uc2 * C.bank gov says current reserves level "more than enough" (Recasts with \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves drop)\par \par \uc2 By Tabita Diela and Gayatri Suroyo\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, April 2 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped by some $9 billion in March, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Thursday, as \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 intensified market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage the depreciation in the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah lost 14% of its value against the dollar in March as investors rushed to liquidate riskier assets amid fear of rapid spread of the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 BI officials have said they had stepped up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and domestic non-deliverable forward markets, as well as snapping up bonds dumped by foreign funds, \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Perry Warjiyo\uc2  has dubbed the "triple \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 Warjiyo told an investor conference call on Thursday that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had dropped to around $121 billion in March, from $130.4 billion at the end of February.\par \par \uc2 He said up to $3 billion was used for debt payments, while the rest was used "to stabilise exchange rate as well as other needs".\par \par \uc2 That was the biggest monthly drop in reserves since September 2011, according to Refinitiv Eikon data.\par \par \uc2 The governor sought to reassure investors that this level was "more than enough" to maintain market stability, saying it was 14% higher than the level considered adequate according to metrics by the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's benchmark 10-year bond yield jumped 1 percentage point in March to close at 7.907%. It rose further to 8.038% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Jakarta's main stock index fell nearly 17% last month.\par \par \uc2 During the call, the governor also reiterated that BI had room to cut interest rates further to cushion the impact of the coronavirus outbreak on Southeast Asia's largest economy.\par \par \uc2 With economic growth hit by the virus outbreak, inflation low and global interest rate policy trending down, Warjiyo said: "Actually we have room for further interest rate cut.\par \par \uc2 "The issue with Indonesia is we have to balance between the need of maintaining inflation and supporting economic growth as well as maintaining the stability of the rupiah."\par \par \uc2 BI has cut it key policy rate six times by a total of 150 basis points since it began an easing cycle last year.\par \par \uc2 Indonesian authorities this week rolled out nearly $25 billion of additional spending on healthcare, social welfare programme and economic stimulus.\par \par \uc2 The country has reported 1,790 coronavirus cases and 170 deaths. (Reporting by Tabita Diela and Gayatri Suroyo; Editing by Alex Richardson) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-4-2T13:43:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200402eg4202abz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
