\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken as rate-cut bets rise in Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 08:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * S.Korean won loses 1%, most among Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * More easing from central banks expected - DBS analysts\par     * Markets pricing in 100 basis point cut by U.S. Fed\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Anushka Trivedi\par     March 12 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on\par Thursday, as expectations rose for rate cuts by central banks in\par the region after world health officials called the coronavirus\par outbreak a pandemic.\par     Rattling already nervy markets, U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par suspended travel from most European countries for a month, which\par threatens to cause more disruptions to trade and the world\par economy.\par     Following the news, odds of a one percentage point cut to\par interest rates at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy review next week\par climbed, while the dollar declined 1% against the yen and\par the 10-year U.S. Treasuries yield fell slightly.\par \par     DBS analysts said in a note that more easing could be\par expected from central banks over the next few weeks, including\par in emerging markets.\par     The Indonesian, Taiwan and Philippine central banks are set\par to hold their monetary policy meetings next week.\par     "With financial conditions still tight, we suspect that\par several 2008-09 crisis era options will also be explored," they\par said.  \par     Singapore's president said the city-state would consider\par tapping national reserves to fund a second economic package,\par which would be the first such move since 2009.\par     Several economists have trimmed their 2020 growth forecasts\par for the trade-reliant economy, citing disruption from the\par epidemic and weakness in the local dollar.\par     This could see its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  re-centre the Singapore\par dollar-NEER policy band lower, DBS analysts said. SGD-NEER\par refers to the exchange rate of the Singapore dollar managed\par against a trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The Singapore dollar was trading 0.4% lower, while\par the Indonesian rupiah weakened 0.9% to 14,465 against\par the dollar. \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  acted on its promised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to steady the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid capital outflows by purchasing 4\par trillion rupiah ($276.53 million) worth of government bonds in\par an auction.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  may conduct a second auction later in the\par afternoon session, an official said.  \par     Other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also took a bearing, with the Indian\par rupee and the Thai baht sliding 0.7% and 0.4%,\par respectively.    \par     South Korea, the country with the largest outbreak in Asia\par outside China, saw its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaken 1%, the most\par among Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .        \par     The Philippine peso dropped 0.6% after the senate\par went into lockdown on Thursday, with President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rodrigo Duterte\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par set to undergo testing for the virus.\par     Investors now await a meeting of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (\f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2 ), which is all but certain to unveil new stimulus measures\par later in the day, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  surprised markets\par with a 50 basis point rate cut on Wednesday.\par     Some analysts have questioned the effectiveness of these\par rate cuts, saying they "may provide a temporary relief in the\par credit markets, but will not solve the underlying issue of the\par rapidly spreading virus around the world", CMC Markets Singapore\par analyst Margaret Yang Yan said. \par        \par     ($1 = 14,465.0000 rupiah)   \par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0537 GMT.\par     \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen                    103.970     104.53        +0.54\par  Sing dlr                     1.401       1.3950        -0.42\par  Taiwan dlr                   30.138      30.095        -0.14\par  Korean won                   1205.100    1193          -1.00\par  Baht                         31.550      31.41         -0.44\par  Peso                         50.940      50.63         -0.61\par  Rupiah                       14465.000   14340         -0.86\par  Rupee                        74.145      73.65         -0.67\par  Ringgit                      4.250       4.237         -0.31\par  Yuan                         6.975       6.9603        -0.21\par                                                         \par  Change so far in 2020                                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                      Latest bid 