\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  steps up  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , unveils stimulus to curb market outflows\b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 12:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * C.bank vows increased market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid volatility\par \par \uc2 * BI cuts RRR in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rupiah\par \par \uc2 * Rupiah, stock market cut losses after announcement (Adds finance minister and stock exchange comments, closing prices)\par \par \uc2 By Tabita Diela\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, March 2 (Reuters) - Indonesia unveiled new measures on Monday to stabilise its financial markets and support growth in Southeast Asia's largest economy, amid capital outflows linked to the coronavirus outbreak as it reported its first confirmed cases.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 will increase market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , cut reserve requirements and relax rules for domestic non-deliverable forward (DNDF) transactions to support the rupiah and bonds, Governor \uc2 Perry Warjiyo\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Separately, Finance Minister \uc2 Sri Mulyani Indrawati\uc2  said import rules for raw materials will be eased as stocks in factories were low amid a trade slowdown due to the global spread of the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 In financial markets, Indonesia's stock exchange (IDX) on Monday suspended all short selling until further notice.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah, which this year had been the best performing among emerging Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell 4% last week and a further 0.5% earlier on Monday to 14,415 - its weakest since May 2019 - after Indonesia announced its first confirmed coronavirus cases.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered to 14,260 following the new measures, posting a 0.6% gain by closing, but the stock index extended losses to 1.7%. The index fell 7.3% last week.\par \par \uc2 "In Indonesia, we're taking this seriously. We assess from time to time so that the impact of COVID-19 to the stability of our economy can be mitigated," Warjiyo said, referring to the global outbreak caused by the virus.\par \par \uc2 He said the impact on Indonesia's economy would be less pronounced than countries like Japan, South Korea and Singapore.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would increase the volume of its "triple" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , DNDF and bond markets so investors "remain confident that BI is always in the market to do its job", Warjyo said.\par \par \uc2 The level of reserves in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that banks must park at BI would be cut by 400 basis points (bps) to 4%, a measure that would pump $3.2 billion into the banking system starting on March 16, Warjiyo said.\par \par \uc2 A similar requirement for rupiah savings would also be cut by 50 bps for banks that lend to exporters and importers starting on April 1 and be effective for nine months, he said.\par \par \uc2 BI will also allow domestic NDF transactions to be based on sales of government bonds by foreign investors, if the proceeds are placed in a rupiah savings account, Warjiyo said, arguing that some foreign investors were looking to reinvest once market volatility subsided.\par \par \uc2 Last month, BI cut interest rates by 25 bps, its fifth rate cut since May, to mitigate the economic impact of the virus outbreak. It also trimmed its 2020 gross domestic product growth outlook to a range of 5.0%-5.4% from 5.1%-5.5%.\par \par \uc2 The government also announced a nearly $750 million stimulus package to support domestic consumption and tourism.\par \par \uc2 Minister Indrawati said more tax breaks could be provided.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Laksono Widodo, a director at IDX, said although short selling did not contribute significantly to the stock market's recent plunge, the measure was taken to prevent further instability.\par \par \uc2 "We don't want people to take advantage of the situation and make conditions worse," he said. (Additional reporting by Maikel Jefriando, Fransiska Nangoy and Bernadette Christina Munthe Writing by Gayatri Suroyo Editing by Robert Birsel and Emelia Sithole-Matarise) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-2T12:56:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200302eg3201pvt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
