\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Virus worries rout Indonesian bonds, rupiah and stocks\b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2020\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah down 2.2% vs dollar, sits at six month low\par \par \uc2 * Stock market plunges\par \par \uc2 * Bond yields jump 30bps in two days (Writes through to add \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock market moves, analyst quotes and background)\par \par \uc2 By Gayatri Suroyo and Tom Westbrook\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA/SINGAPORE, Feb 28 (Reuters) - Indonesian bonds, stocks and its rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plummeted on Friday as foreign investors dumped risky assets on fears the world is on the cusp of a pandemic.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah dropped 2%, its steepest fall in more than eight years, benchmark 10-year bond prices suffered their steepest plunge in a year and the stock market fell to an almost three-year low.\par \par \uc2 "It's a big wave out of the high yielders," said Stephen Innes, Asia-Pacific market strategist at AxiCorp. "We're just seeing a complete de-risking of every asset."\par \par \uc2 Years of low and falling interest rates around the globe had driven billions of dollars in foreign money into countries such as Indonesia and Mexico in search of higher yields.\par \par \uc2 However, the resultant heavy presence of foreigners in Indonesia's debt market and relatively low \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have left it vulnerable as investors seek to reduce risk en masse.\par \par \uc2 The yield on benchmark 10-year bonds, which rises when prices fall, jumped 17 basis points to 6.887%. It has risen almost 30 basis points in two days. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has lost 5% against the dollar in little more than a week.\par \par \uc2 "Risk sentiment is fragile, and countries where risk premia was too low are more affected, with Indonesia being one of them," said Ashish Agrawal, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and emerging markets' macro research for Asia at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Flows point to a massive liquidiation of foreign holdings, which comprise a bit more than a third of Indonesian debt.\par \par \uc2 Non-resident investors had already sold 16.43 trillion rupiah ($1.2 billion) of tradable government bonds over the first three days of the week, according to the latest government data.\par \par \uc2 Price moves this week prompted \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilise yields and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Bond markets and especially \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to face pressure as \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are limited," Nomura analysts said in a note on Friday, which disclosed that the bank had, on Feb. 20, closed a bet that the rupiah would rise against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Our decision to exit our position was driven by the deterioration of the global risk environment and concerns that BI (\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 ) would allow the rupiah to weaken," the note said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  often uses a domestic version of the non-deliverable forwards to influence the rupiah's value. But analysts said the low auction volumes of such contracts only increased worries about BI's ammunition.\par \par \uc2 It sold about $1.8 billion in forwards on Wednesday and Thursday, a drop in the ocean compared with the more than $70 billion of foreign holdings of rupiah bonds.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 14,200 rupiah)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Gayatri Suroyo and Fransiska Nangoy in Jakarta and Vidya Ranganathan and Tom Westbrook in Singapore; Editing by Christian Schmollinger and Emelia Sithole-Matarise) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-28T10:58:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200228eg2s01j8x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
