\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fears of virus spread pound Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 ; ringgit tumbles\b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2020\par 07:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * S. Korean won drops to near six-month low\par     * Political uncertainty sparks selling pressure on ringgit\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bond markets\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Shriya Ramakrishnan\par     Feb 24 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  posted steep\par losses against the dollar on Monday as a rapid surge in\par coronavirus infections and deaths outside mainland China\par heightened fears of a pandemic and sent investors fleeing to\par safe-haven assets.\par     Italy, South Korea and Iran reported a sharp rise in\par infections over the weekend. South Korea put the country on high\par alert, while Italy began sealing off the worst affected towns\par and banning public events after a spike in the number of virus\par cases to above 150.\par     The South Korean won plunged 0.8% to a near\par six-month low against the greenback, in tandem with sharp falls\par in local equities.\par     South Korea's vice finance minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kim Yong-beom\f28 \uc2 \f2  said a set\par of measures would be announced soon to boost exports,\par investments and domestic demand and that any "herd-like"\par speculative moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets would be stemmed.\par \par     "There's a sobering realisation that this could really\par impact hard and fast... truly the notion of China sneezing and\par everyone catching a cold, that becomes a real fright for anyone\par watching this," said Vishnu Varathan, head of economics at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in Singapore.\par     Against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the dollar crept back\par toward an almost three-year peak touched last week amid a\par broader risk-aversion.\par     The Indonesian rupiah, which has held up better so\par far this year against its Asian peers due to its carry trade\par appeal, fell 0.9% to its weakest level in more than a month\par during the session despite an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , domestic non-deliverable forward and bond markets amid\par outflows related to fears of the spread of COVID-19 in South\par Korea, an official told Reuters on Monday.\par     The Chinese yuan inched lower against the dollar,\par while the Singapore dollar fell 0.3%. \par     The Thai baht dropped as much as 0.5% to hit a near\par nine-month low, with investors largely shrugging off an\par unexpected rise in exports for the trade-reliant economy in\par January.\par     \par     POLITICAL TURMOIL GRIPS MALAYSIAN RINGGIT\par     Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad has submitted his\par letter of resignation to the king, his office said on Monday,\par amid talk of forming a new governing coalition.\par     The uncertainty added pressure on the ringgit, with\par the local unit sliding 0.8% to 4.22 per dollar, its weakest\par level in five-and-a-half months. \par     Yields on the country's 10-year government bonds\par also rose 6.1 bps to 2.972, as of Monday's open. \par     Malaysian bonds, long a favourite with foreign investors,\par have seen net heavy inflows between November and January. \par     \par \par    \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     \par  Change on the day at   0616 GMT                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              111.570     111.57        +0.00\par  Sing dlr               1.403       1.3981        -0.31\par  Taiwan dlr             30.440      30.403        -0.12\par  Korean won             1219.300    1209.2        -0.83\par  Baht                   31.735      31.61         -0.39\par  Peso                   50.960      50.89         -0.14\par  Rupiah                 13890.000   13760         -0.94\par  Rupee                  71.838      71.65         -0.26\par  Ringgit                4.220       4.188         -0.76\par  Yuan                   7.035       7.0265        -0.13\par                                                   \par  Change so far in 2020                            \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End 2019      Pct Move\par  Japan yen              111.570     108.61        -2.65\par  Sing dlr               1.403       1.3444        -4.14\par  Taiwan dlr             30.440      30.106        -1.10\par  Korean won             1219.300    1156.40       -5.16\par  Baht                   31.735      29.91         -5.75\par  Peso                   50.960      50.65         -0.61\par  Rupiah                 13890.000   13880         -0.07\par  Rupee                  71.838      71.38         -0.64\par  Ringgit                4.220       4.0890        -3.10\par  Yuan                   7.035       6.9632        -1.03\par  \par \par  (Reporting by Shriya Ramakrishnan in Bengaluru; Editing by