\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , bond markets amid capital outflows\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2020\par 04:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds trader comment and context)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Feb 24 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , domestic non-deliverable forward (DNDF) and bond markets amid outflows related to fears of the spread of COVID-19 in South Korea, an official told Reuters on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell by 0.9% as of 0331 GMT, the weakest since Jan. 8 and the biggest intraday fall in nearly a year. The main stock index fell more than 1%, while yields of government bonds with 1 year- and 3 year-tenure rose.\par \par \uc2 "There are outflows in the bond (market) and banks are short covering," Nanang Hendarsah, \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's head of monetary management said by text message.\par \par \uc2 "Because of the jump in virus cases in Korea during the weekend. It's to do with flight to quality away from EM assets," he added, referring to emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 A trader in Jakarta said BI was "being aggressive" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond and DNDF markets, but liquidity in spot \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading remained "a bit difficult".\par \par \uc2 A surge of infections in South Korea and Italy, and an alarming rise in the death toll in Iran over the weekend, triggered steep falls in Asian share markets and Wall Street stock futures on Monday as investors fled to safe havens.\par \par \uc2 BI cut interest rates last week to ward off the impact of the coronavirus epidemic on the domestic economy, a fifth cut since May 2019.\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Perry Warjiyo\uc2  said after announcing the rate cut BI was committed to stabilising the rupiah exchange rate in the market.\par \par \uc2 BI had bought a net total of 61.5 trillion rupiah ($4.43 billion) of sovereign bonds to stabilise yields, 27 trillion rupiah of which was made during capital outflows related to coronavirus fears earlier this month, the governor said on Thursday. ($1 = 13,890.0000 rupiah) (Reporting by Gayatri Suroyo and Fransiska Nangoy; Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-24T04:41:51.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200224eg2o00f1p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
