\par\par \b \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt\b0\par\par\uc2 4,681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2020\par 08:00\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2020 \par \par \uc2 TIDM42BI\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 4070C\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 07 February 2020\par \par \uc2 PRICING SUPPLEMENT\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 Global Debt Program\par \par \uc2 Series No.: 742\par \par \uc2 IDR 1,357,500,000,000 5.500 percent Notes due February 7, 2023 (the "Notes")\par \par \uc2 payable in United States Dollars\par \par \uc2 Issue Price: 100.00 percent\par \par \uc2 Application has been made for the Notes to be admitted to the Official List of the \uc2 Financial Conduct Authority\uc2  and to trading on the \uc2 London Stock Exchange plc\uc2 's Regulated Market\par \par \uc2 Deutsche Bank\par \par \uc2 The date of this Pricing Supplement is as of February 4, 2020\par \par \uc2 Terms used herein shall be deemed to be defined as such for the purposes of the Terms and Conditions (the "Conditions") set forth in the Prospectus dated January 8, 2001 (the "Prospectus") (which for the avoidance of doubt does not constitute a prospectus for the purposes of Part VI of the United Kingdom Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 or a base prospectus for the purposes of Regulation (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) 2017/1129). This Pricing Supplement must be read in conjunction with the Prospectus. This document is issued to give details of an issue by the \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  (the "Bank") under its Global Debt Program and to provide information supplemental to the Prospectus. Complete information in respect of the Bank and this offer of the Notes is only available on the basis of the combination of this Pricing Supplement and the Prospectus.\par \par \uc2 MiFID II product governance / Retail investors, professional investors and ECPs target market - See "General Information-Additional Information Regarding the Notes-Matters relating to MiFID II" below.\par \par \uc2 Terms and Conditions\par \par \uc2 The following items under this heading "Terms and Conditions" are the particular terms which relate to the issue the subject of this Pricing Supplement. These are the only terms which form part of the form of Notes for such issue. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  1.    Series No.:                      742 \par  2.    Aggregate Principal Amount:      IDR 1,357,500,000,000 \par  3.    Issue Price:                           IDR 1,357,500,000,000 which \par                                             amount represents 100.00 percent \par                                            of the Aggregate Principal Amount. \par                                             The Issue Price will be payable \par                                               in USD in the amount of USD \par                                              100,000,000 at the agreed rate \par                                                of 13,575 IDR per one USD. \par  4.    Issue Date:                      February 7, 2020 \par  5.    Form of Notes \par         (Condition 1(a)):                Registered only, as further \par                                          provided in paragraph 9(c) of \par                                          "Other Relevant Terms" below. \par  6.    Authorized Denomination(s) \par          (Condition 1(b)):               IDR 10,000,000 and integral \par                                          multiples thereof \par  7.    Specified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         (Condition 1(d)):                The lawful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the \par                                          Republic of Indonesia ("Indonesian \par                                          Rupiah" or "IDR"), provided \par                                          that all payments in respect \par                                          of the Notes will be made in \par                                          United States Dollars ("U.S.$" \par                                          or "USD") \par  8.    Specified Principal Payment \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)):      USD \par  9.    Specified Interest Payment \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          USD \par         (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)): \par  10.   Maturity Date \par         (Condition 6(a); Fixed            February 7, 2023 \par         Interest Rate): \par  11.   Interest Basis \par         (Condition 5):                   Fixed Interest Rate (Condition \par                                          5(I)) \par  12.   Interest Commencement Date \par         (Condition 5(III)):               February 7, 2020 \par  13.   Fixed Interest Rate (Condition   Condition 5(I) as amended and \par         5(I)):                           supplemented below, shall apply \par                                          to the Notes. The bases of the \par                                          Calculation of the Interest \par                                          Amount, Interest Payment Dates \par                                          and default interest are as \par                                          set out below. \par  \par          (a) Interest Rate:              5.500 percent per annum \par        (b) Business Day Convention:     Following Business Day Convention \par        (c) Fixed Rate Interest \par         Payment Date(s):                  Annually on each February 7, \par                                           commencing on February 7, 2021 \par                                           and ending on, and including, \par                                           the Maturity Date. \par                                           Each Interest Payment Date is \par                                           subject to adjustment in accordance \par                                           with the Following Business \par                                           Day Convention with no adjustment \par                                           to the amount of interest otherwise \par                                           calculated. \par        (d) Interest Period:             Each period from and including \par                                          each Interest Payment Date to \par                                          but excluding the next following \par                                          Interest Payment Date, provided \par                                          that the initial Interest Period \par                                          will commence on and include \par                                          the Interest Commencement Date, \par                                          and the final Interest Period \par                                          will end on but exclude the \par                                          Maturity Date. \par                                          For the purposes of the calculation \par                                          of the Interest Amount payable \par                                          for any Interest Period, there \par                                          shall be no adjustment pursuant \par                                          to the Business Day Convention \par                                          specified above. \par        (e) Fixed Rate Day Count \par         Fraction(s):                     Actual/Actual ICMA \par        (f) Calculation of Interest      As soon as practicable and in \par         Amount:                          accordance with the procedure \par                                          specified herein, the Calculation \par                                          Agent will determine the IDR \par                                          Rate (as defined below) and \par                                          calculate the amount of interest \par                                          payable (the "Interest Amount") \par                                          with respect to each minimum \par                                          Authorized Denomination for \par                                          the relevant Interest Period. \par                                          The Interest Amount with respect \par                                          to any Interest Period shall \par                                          be a USD amount calculated on \par                                          the relevant Rate Fixing Date \par                                          (as defined below) as follows: \par                                          5.500% times the minimum Authorized \par                                          Denomination \par  \par                                          times \par  \par                                          the Fixed Rate Day Count Fraction \par  \par                                          divided by \par  \par                                          the IDR Rate \par  \par                                          (and rounding, if necessary, \par                                          the entire resulting figure \par                                          to the nearest two decimal places, \par                                          with USD 0.005 being rounded \par                                          upwards). \par  \par                                          The "IDR Rate" means the rate \par                                          determined by the Calculation \par                                          Agent that is equal to the USD/IDR \par                                          weighted average spot rate in \par                                          the interbank market, based \par                                          on traded USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                          exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions during \par                                          a specified time period which \par                                          are captured on a real time \par                                          basis, expressed as the amount \par                                          of IDR per one USD, for settlement \par                                          in two Fixing Business Days, \par                                          as published by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                          as the "Jakarta Interbank Spot \par                                          Dollar Rate USD - IDR", which \par                                          appears on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                          website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), or as \par                                          published on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                          Screen JISDOR Page (or any replacement \par                                          page or replacement service \par                                          as may be implemented for the \par                                          purposes of displaying the USD/IDR \par                                          weighted average spot rate), \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                          or as otherwise made available \par                                          by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its successor \par                                          as administrator), at approximately \par                                          10:00 a.m., Jakarta time, on \par                                          the Rate Fixing Date. Fallback \par                                          Provisions apply as set out \par                                          below. \par                                         The "Rate Fixing Date" means \par                                          the date that is five (5) Fixing \par                                          Business Days prior to the applicable \par                                          Fixed Rate Interest Payment \par                                          Date or Maturity Date, as the \par                                          case may be. The Rate Fixing \par                                          Date shall be subject to adjustment \par                                          as follows: if the scheduled \par                                          date of the Rate Fixing Date \par                                          is not a Relevant Business Day, \par                                          then the Rate Fixing Date will \par                                          be the first preceding day that \par                                          is a Relevant Business Day. \par                                          "Fixing Business Day" means \par                                          a day (other than a Saturday \par                                          or a Sunday) on which banks \par                                          and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets \par                                          are open for business in Jakarta. \par                                         "Fallback Provisions": Should \par                                          no USD/IDR weighted average \par                                          spot rate appear on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                          website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ) as the \par                                          "Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar \par                                          Rate USD - IDR", or on Thomson \par                                          Reuters Screen JISDOR Page (or \par                                          on such replacement page or \par                                          replacement service as described \par                                          above), or be otherwise made \par                                          available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par                                          (or its successor as administrator), \par                                          on the Rate Fixing Date, then \par                                          the IDR Rate for such Rate Fixing \par                                          Date shall be determined by \par                                          the Calculation Agent by requesting \par                                          quotations for the mid USD/IDR \par                                          spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate from \par                                          five banks active in the USD/IDR \par                                          \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                          markets as selected by the Calculation \par                                          Agent (such banks, the "Reference \par                                          Banks") either (i) at or about \par                                          10:00 a.m. Jakarta time on the \par                                          first day (other than a Saturday \par                                          or a Sunday) following the Rate \par                                          Fixing Date, if such day is \par                                          a Relevant Business Day or (ii) \par                                          at or about 10:00 a.m. Jakarta \par                                          time on the Rate Fixing Date, \par                                          if the first day (other than \par                                          a Saturday or a Sunday) following \par                                          the Rate Fixing Date is not \par                                          a Relevant Business Day. \par                                         If five or four quotations are \par                                          provided by Reference Banks \par                                          as requested, the IDR Rate shall \par                                          be the arithmetic mean (rounded \par                                          to the nearest whole IDR, with \par                                          IDR 0.5 being rounded upwards) \par                                          of the remaining three or two \par                                          such quotations (expressed as \par                                          the number of IDR per one USD), \par                                          as the case may be, after disregarding \par                                          the highest quotation and the \par                                          lowest quotation; provided, \par                                          that if two or more such quotations \par                                          are the highest such quotations, \par                                          then only one of such quotations \par                                          shall be disregarded; and provided \par                                          further, that if two or more \par                                          such quotations are the lowest \par                                          such quotations, then only one \par                                          of such lowest quotations shall \par                                          be disregarded. \par                                          If only three or two quotations \par                                          are provided as requested, the \par                                          IDR Rate shall be the arithmetic \par                                          mean (rounded to the nearest \par                                          whole IDR, with IDR 0.5 being \par                                          rounded upwards) of such quotations \par                                          (expressed as the number of \par                                          IDR per one USD). \par                                          If only one or no quotations \par                                          are provided as requested, or \par                                          if the Calculation Agent determines \par                                          in its sole discretion that \par                                          no suitable Reference Banks \par                                          active in the USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                          or \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets \par                                          will provide quotations, the \par                                          Calculation Agent shall be entitled \par                                          to calculate the IDR Rate acting \par                                          in good faith in a commercially \par                                          reasonable manner, having taken \par                                          into account relevant market \par                                          practice, by reference to such \par                                          additional sources as it deems \par                                          appropriate; and in such case \par                                          the Calculation Agent shall \par                                          notify the Bank and the Global \par                                          Agent as soon as reasonably \par                                          practicable that the IDR Rate \par                                          is to be so determined. \par        (g) Calculation Agent:           See "8. Identity of Calculation \par                                          Agent" under "Other Relevant \par                                          Terms" \par        (h) Notification:                If the Interest Amount payable \par                                          on any Fixed Rate Interest Payment \par                                          Date or the Redemption Amount, \par                                          as the case may be, is calculated \par                                          in any manner other than by \par                                          utilizing the USD/IDR reference \par                                          rate that appears on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                          website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), or on \par                                          Thomson Reuters Screen JISDOR \par                                          Page (or on such replacement \par                                          page as described above), or \par                                          as otherwise made available \par                                          by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its successor \par                