\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken as virus worries pound yuan\b0\par\par\uc2 663 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2020\par 08:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Chinese yuan down 1.2%, past symbolic 7 per dollar\par     * More than $420 bln wiped off Chinese equities benchmark\par index\par     * Indonesian rupiah's 0.6% tumble draws cenbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par \par     By Rashmi Ashok\par     Feb 3 (Reuters) - The yuan weakened over 1% in onshore trade\par on Monday after Chinese markets reopened following an extended\par Lunar New Year break, pulling down already bruised Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as worries over the coronavirus outbreak cast a pall\par over the region.\par     Trading for the first time since Jan. 23, the onshore yuan\par  shed 1.2% to trade at 7.019 against the dollar, the\par weakest since Dec. 12, 2019, as the death toll in China from the\par fast-spreading virus rose to 361 as of Sunday.\par     In a show of support, \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unexpectedly\par lowered the interest rates on reverse repurchase agreements and\par also injected a total of 1.2 trillion yuan ($173.81 billion)\par into money markets on Monday.\par     The measures, however, did little to assuage markets.\par Investors shaved off about $420 billion from the benchmark\par Shanghai Composite index, while yields on the country's\par 30-year government bonds fell.\par     "The coordinated and pre-emptive measures by Beijing will go\par a long way to soften the blow, but confidence remains fragile\par amid high uncertainty," Lavanya Venkateswaran, economist at\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Asia & Oceania Treasury Department said.\par     Knock-on effects from the yuan's dive and worries over the\par outbreak hurting demand from China kept most regional units\par under pressure.\par     The Thai baht weakened 0.1%. The region's best\par performer across the last two years, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has shed over\par 4% since the year began.\par     Last week, the Thai Tourism Ministry warned that reduced\par travel from China alone could result in 50 billion baht ($1.52\par billion) of lost tourism revenue.\par     The Malaysian ringgit eased 0.4% while the Taiwan\par dollar and South Korean won lost about 0.3%\par each against the dollar.\par     Even the Indian rupee eased, despite data from a\par private survey which showed manufacturing activity in the\par country expanded at its quickest pace in nearly eight years in\par January.\par     The Indonesian rupiah tumbled nearly 0.6% to trade\par at 13,725 against the dollar \u8212\'20\'14 weakest in nearly three weeks \u8212\'20\'14\par despite the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepping in to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     An official said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in spot\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading as well as domestic non-deliverable\par forward and bond markets to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , whose fall\par he attributed to the sudden drop in Chinese markets.\par \par     So far this year, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the region's best\par performer and sole gainer, firming 1%, as a series of rate hikes\par across 2018 to defend against capital outflows continue to lend\par support.\par     \par The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the\par dollar at 0613 GMT.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              108.480     108.38        -0.09\par  Sing dlr               1.368       1.3648        -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr             30.298      30.250        -0.16\par  Korean won             1195.500    1191.8        -0.31\par  Baht                   31.180      31.15         -0.10\par  Peso                   50.980      51            +0.04\par  Rupiah                 13725.000   13650         -0.55\par  Rupee                  71.578      71.34         -0.33\par  Ringgit                4.111       4.095         -0.39\par  Yuan                   7.015       6.9368        -1.11\par                                                   \par  Change so far in 2020                            \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End 2019      Pct Move\par  Japan yen              108.480     108.61        +0.12\par  Sing dlr               1.368       1.3444        -1.75\par  Taiwan dlr             30.298      30.106        -0.63\par  Korean won             1195.500    1156.40       -3.27\par  Baht                   31.180      29.91         -4.07\par  Peso                   50.980      50.65         -0.65\par  Rupiah                 13725.000   13880         +1.13\par  Rupee                  71.578      71.38         -0.28\par  Ringgit                4.111       4.0890        -0.54\par  Yuan                   7.015       6.9632        -0.73\par  \par \par  (Reporting by Rashmi Ashok in Bengaluru; Editing by Shounak\par Dasgupta)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-3T08:03:16.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA00