\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to steady rupiah as virus fear unnerves markets\b0\par\par\uc2 540 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2020\par 07:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * C.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spot \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , domestic NDF, bond markets\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's markets fall following drop in Chinese markets\par \par \uc2 * Trader says liquidity is tight in spot market (Adds traders comment, background)\par \par \uc2 By Gayatri Suroyo and Fransiska Nangoy\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Feb 3 (Reuters) - \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spot foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading as well as domestic non-deliverable forward and bond markets on Monday to stabilise the rupiah, an official said, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell 0.5% to the weakest since mid-January.\par \par \uc2 "BI is making sure of rupiah's stability," Nanang Hendarsah, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's head of monetary management, told Reuters by text message.\par \par \uc2 "BI is boldly buying bonds in the secondary market and is offering DNDF (domestic non-deliverable forwards) through 8 brokers," he said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also done in a measured way in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Hendarsah attributed the rupiah's fall in early trade to a drop in China's equities market, which plunged after reopening from a 10-day Lunar New Year holiday amid a rapidly spreading virus epidemic.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan and commodities markets in Shanghai slumped on Monday, on fears the coronavirus epidemic will hit demand in the world's second-largest economy. The death toll in China rose to 361 as of Sunday with the number of confirmed cases rising to more than 17,200.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell as much as 0.5% to 13,725 per dollar by 0442 GMT. So far this year, it has gained 1.1% helped by big inflows.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia is one of Asia's higher-yielding markets and has attracted heavy overseas inflows into its bond markets as investors sought better returns in a world of plunging interest rates.\u8203\'20\'0B\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's benchmark 10-year bond yield jumped to 6.701%, from the previous session's close of 6.645%.\par \par \uc2 The stock market fell 0.5% on Monday and is down 6.6% since mid-January, making it the second-worst performing in Southeast Asia after Manila so far this year.\par \par \uc2 BI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in bonds, DNDF and spot markets almost daily last week, according to a trader in Jakarta, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen focusing most of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond and DNDF markets.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-month DNDF contracts on Monday traded at 13,751 to the dollar, stronger than comparable offshore non-delivereable forwards at 13,840.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have helped keep the rupiah mostly stable in recent weeks, the trader said, but dollar liquidity in the spot market is tight.\par \par \uc2 "BI prefers to do their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through DNDF now, but most of the offshore traders are seeking dollar in the spot market, which currently is a bit illiquid," the trader said.\par \par \uc2 BI sold DNDF contracts worth more than $380 million early on Monday, the trader said, adding to around $450 million sold on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes the pressure on the rupiah is temporary.\par \par \uc2 "We believe the rupiah's weakness is temporary because fundamentally, the rupiah will be supported by a narrowing current account deficit, low and stable inflation and resilient growth," Hendarsah said.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Vidya Ranganathan and Jacqueline Wong) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-3T07:06:57.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200203eg2300o2p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
