\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank\uc2  says  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  to steady the rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2020\par 03:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Feb 3 (Reuters) - \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in spot foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading as well as domestic non-deliverable forward and bond markets on Mondau to stabilise the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which fell by 0.4% to the weakest since mid-January, an official said.\par \par \uc2 "BI is making sure of rupiah's stability," Nanang Hendarsah, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's head of monetary management, told Reuters by text message.\par \par \uc2 "BI is boldly buying bonds in the secondary market and is offering DNDF (domestic non-deliverable forward) through 8 brokers," he said, adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also done in a measured way in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Hendarsah attributed the rupiah's fall to touch 13,718 a dollar in early Monday trading to a drop in China's equity market, which plunged amid a rapidly spreading virus epidemic. (Reporting by Gayatri Suroyo; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-2-3T03:44:04.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200203eg2300a3x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
