\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if rupiah becomes too strong - governor\b0\par\par\uc2 152 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2020\par 07:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Jan 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stand ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market should the rupiah \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  become too strong, although its current level is still fine, the bank's governor told lawmakers on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "So far, the rupiah's appreciation has a positive impact on the economy," \uc2 Perry Warjiyo\uc2  told a hearing of parliament's financial commission.\par \par \uc2 "If, later on, it strengthens too far and it affects the economy negatively, we will not hesitate to guide it towards its fundamentals, using market mechanism."\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has rallied in recent weeks and closed last week at its strongest in almost two years, at 13,565 to the dollar. On Monday, it weakened slightly, to stand at 13,605 by 0612 GMT. (Reporting by Tabita Diela; Writing by Gayatri Suroyo; Editing by Clarence Fernandez) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-1-27T07:20:34.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200127eg1r00gqt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
