\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Most  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  under pressure on rising U.S.-Iran tensions\b0\par\par\uc2 612 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2020\par 06:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Oil price hike weakens Indian rupee, Indonesian rupiah\par     * Rupee hits worst level in more than 7 weeks\par     * Indonesian rupiah down to over 1-week low\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Aby Jose Koilparambil\par     Jan 6 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on Monday\par as risk appetite in the region was dented further, with\par heightened tensions between the United States and Iran sending\par crude oil and safe-haven gold prices higher.\par     The U.S. and Iran are locked in a war of words, exchanging\par threats of attacks on each other and stoking concerns of an\par extended conflict, after a top Iranian military commander was\par killed in Iraq by an American drone strike on Friday.\par \par     Oil prices have surged more than 2%, sending Brent futures\par above the $70 per barrel mark, following a 3% rise on Friday,\par after the killing of the Iranian commander \f28 \uc2 \f2 Qassem Soleimani\f28 \uc2 \f2  and\par the ensuing rise in tensions. \par     "The Middle East tensions have led Brent crude prices\par towards $70/bbl, up from just above $60 a month ago... The last\par thing markets want is a move from a tit-for-tat (Sino-U.S.)\par tariff war to sabre-rattling in the Gulf," said DBS Group\par Research analysts in a note.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of India and Indonesia - two major Asian\par economies exposed to the impact of oil imports on their current\par account deficit - wilted under pressure.\par     The Indian rupee weakened as much as 0.4% to its\par worst level in more than seven weeks, while the Indonesian\par rupiah fell about 0.3% to a one-week low of 13,920\par against the dollar.\par     Also, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , domestic non-deliverable forward (DNDF) and bond\par markets to stabilise movements, the head of its monetary\par management, told Reuters.\par     "The key question is whether the oil market would be able to\par absorb any potential supply losses, and the simple answer is\par that it will obviously depend on the scale of any disruptions,"\par ING analysts wrote in a note.\par     The Malaysian ringgit, the Philippine peso\par and the Korean won weakened about 0.2% each, while\par the Singapore dollar fell slightly.  \par     The weakness in the Chinese yuan was relatively\par marginal - a drop of about 0.1% -  even as investors await more\par concrete details of the first phase of the Sino-U.S. trade deal,\par scheduled for mid-month.\par     Meanwhile, the Taiwan dollar and the Thai baht\par  strengthened marginally. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  Change on the day at   0512 GMT                  \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              108.040     108.08        +0.04\par  Sing dlr               1.350       1.3496        -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr             30.080      30.105        +0.08\par  Korean won             1168.800    1167.1        -0.15\par  Baht                   30.130      30.14         +0.03\par  Peso                   51.190      51.1          -0.18\par  Rupiah                 13955.000   13920         -0.25\par  Rupee                  7