\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  firm as dovish Fed weighs on dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 2019\par 07:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Taiwan dollar hits strongest level in near 1-1/2 years\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine c.bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate decision awaited\par     * S.Korean won snaps three straight sessions of losses\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Shreya Mariam Job\par     Dec 12 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firmed on Thursday\par against a weaker dollar that was pressured by dovish comments\par from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  after the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pushed back\par expectations of a rate hike anytime soon. \par     In its final policy meeting of a tumultuous year, when it\par was spurred to cut interest rates three times to forestall a\par slowdown fuelled largely by President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's trade war,\par the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  struck a remarkably sanguine tone,\par confident the actions it had taken so far are working.   \par \par     The dovish remarks by the Fed put pressure on the greenback,\par sending the dollar index to a four-month low, providing\par support to emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Powell has focused on sanguine inflationary trends ...\par whether we look at inflation expectations or even the Fed's own\par projections on core personal consumption expenditure,\par "sustained" (rise in inflation) isn't happening anytime soon, if\par at all," Chris Weston, head of research at Pepperstone said in a\par note. \par     The Korean won strengthened the most in the\par region after it firmed 0.7%, wiping out weakness logged earlier\par this week.\par     Investor sentiment also improved after the senior deputy\par governor of the Bank of Korea said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expects\par global uncertainties to ease further.\par     Meanwhile, the Taiwan dollar firmed as much as 0.6%\par to its strongest level since July 2018. \par     However, the rest of the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  witnessed only\par modest gains, given the Dec. 15 deadline for imposition of new\par tariffs on Chinese good by the United States. \par     Trump is expected to meet with top trade advisers on\par Thursday to discuss planned Dec. 15 tariffs on some $160 billion\par in Chinese goods, three sources familiar with the plans said.\par \par     The Chinese yuan remained stable, edging 0.1%\par higher against the dollar. \par     The Philippine peso also strengthened 0.1% ahead of\par its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meeting later in the day, where policy rates\par are expected to be kept steady.\par     The Philippine government cut its growth goals for 2021 and\par 2022 due to rising global uncertainties, including the U.S.-Sino\par trade tensions.\par     The Indonesian rupiah traded flat after Reuters\par reported that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is set to hold two\par non-deliverable forward auctions every day from 2020.  \par     The move was a bid to increase market liquidity and not a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's head of monetary\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Thursday.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     \par  Change on the day at 0547 GMT                    \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              108.590     108.54        -0.05\par  Sing dlr               1.356       1.3569        +0.07\par  Taiwan dlr             30.344      30.505        +0.53\par  Korean won             1186.100    1194.7        +0.73\par  Baht                   30.205      30.25         +0.15\par  Peso                   50.700      50.77         +0.14\par  Rupiah                 14030.000   14030         +0.00\par  Rupee                  70.695      70.84         +0.20\par  Ringgit                4.152       4.163         +0.26\par  Yuan                   7.032       7.0386        +0.10\par                                                   \par  Change so far in 2019                            \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End 2018      Pct Move\par  Japan yen              108.590     109.56        +0.89\par  Sing dlr               1.356       1.3627        +0.49\par  Taiwan dlr             30.344      30.733        +1.28\par  Korean won             1186.100    1115.70       -5.94\par  Baht                   30.205      32.55         +7.76\par  Peso                   50.700      52.47         +3.49\par  Rupiah                 14030.000   14375         +2.46\par  Rupee                  70.695      69.77         -1.31\par  Ringgit                4.152       4.1300        -0.53\par  Yuan                   7.032       6.8730        -2.26\par  \par \par  (Reporting by Shreya Mariam Job in Bengaluru, Editing by Sherry\par Jacob-Phillips)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-12-12T07:59:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020191212efcc00p5l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
