\par\par \b \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt\b0\par\par\uc2 3,794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2019\par 08:00\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2019 \par \par \uc2 TIDM42BI\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 4814I\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 08 August 2019\par \par \uc2 PRICING SUPPLEMENT\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 Global Debt Program\par \par \uc2 Series No.: 717\par \par \uc2 IDR 15,500,000,000 Zero Coupon Notes due August 9, 2022 (the "Notes") payable in Japanese Yen\par \par \uc2 Issue Price: 86.30 percent\par \par \uc2 No application has been made to list the Notes on any stock exchange.\par \par \uc2 HSBC\par \par \uc2 The date of this Pricing Supplement is August 5, 2019\par \par \uc2 Terms used herein shall be deemed to be defined as such for the purposes of the Terms and Conditions (the "Conditions") set forth in the Prospectus dated January 8, 2001 (the "Prospectus") (which for the avoidance of doubt does not constitute a prospectus for the purposes of Part VI of the United Kingdom Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 or a base prospectus for the purposes of Directive 2003/71/EC of the \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  and of the Council). This Pricing Supplement must be read in conjunction with the Prospectus. This document is issued to give details of an issue by the \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  (the "Bank") under its Global Debt Program and to provide information supplemental to the Prospectus. Complete information in respect of the Bank and this offer of the Notes is only available on the basis of the combination of this Pricing Supplement and the Prospectus.\par \par \uc2 Terms and Conditions\par \par \uc2 The following items under this heading "Terms and Conditions" are the particular terms which relate to the issue the subject of this Pricing Supplement. These are the only terms which form part of the form of Notes for such issue. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  1.    Series No.:                         717 \par  2.    Aggregate Principal Amount:         IDR 15,500,000,000 \par  3.    Issue Price:                              IDR 13,376,500,000 which is \par                                                 86.30 percent of the Aggregate \par                                                        Principal Amount. \par                                                 The Issue Price will be payable \par                                                   in JPY in the amount of JPY \par                                                 102,651,261 at the agreed rate \par                                                  of JPY 0.007674 per one IDR. \par  4.    Issue Date:                         August 8, 2019 \par  5.    Form of Notes \par         (Condition 1(a)):                   Bearer only. \par                                             The Notes will initially be \par                                             represented by a temporary global \par                                             note in bearer form (the "Temporary \par                                             Bearer Global Note"). Interests \par                                             in the Temporary Bearer Global \par                                             Note will, not earlier than \par                                             the Exchange Date, be exchangeable \par                                             for interests in a permanent \par                                             global note in bearer form (the \par                                             "Permanent Bearer Global Note"). \par                                             Interests in the Permanent Bearer \par                                             Global Note will be exchangeable \par                                             for definitive Notes in bearer \par                                             form ("Definitive Bearer Notes"), \par                                             in the following circumstances: \par                                             (i) if the Permanent Bearer \par                                             Global Note is held on behalf \par                                             of a clearing system and such \par                                             clearing system is closed for \par                                             business for a continuous period \par                                             of fourteen (14) days (other \par                                             than by reason of holidays, \par                                             statutory or otherwise) or announces \par                                             its intention to permanently \par                                             cease business or does in fact \par                                             do so, by any such holder giving \par                                             written notice to the Global \par                                             Agent; and (ii) at the option \par                                             of any such holder upon not \par                                             less than sixty (60) days' written \par                                             notice to the Bank and the Global \par                                             Agent from Euroclear and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Clearstream\f28 \uc2 \f2  , \par                                             Luxembourg on behalf of such \par                                             holder; provided, that no such \par                                             exchanges will be made by the \par                                             Global Agent, and no Noteholder \par                                             may require such an exchange, \par                                             during a period of fifteen (15) \par                                             days ending on the due date \par                                             for any payment of principal \par                                             on the Notes. \par  6.    Authorized Denomination(s) \par          (Condition 1(b)):                  IDR 50,000,000 and integral \par                                             multiples thereof \par  7.    Specified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         (Condition 1(d)):                   The lawful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the \par                                             Republic of Indonesia ("Indonesian \par                                             Rupiah" or "IDR"), provided \par                                             that all payments in respect \par                                             of the Notes will be made in \par                                             Japanese Yen ("JPY") \par  8.    Specified Principal Payment \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par         (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)):         JPY \par  9.    Specified Interest Payment \par         \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             JPY \par         (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)): \par  10.   Maturity Date \par         (Condition 6(a); Zero Coupon):       August 9, 2022 \par                                              The Maturity Date is subject \par                                              to adjustment in accordance \par                                              with the Modified Following \par                                              Business Day Convention with \par                                              no adjustment to the amount \par                                              of interest otherwise calculated. \par  11.   Interest Basis \par         (Condition 5):                      Zero Coupon (Condition 5(IV)) \par  12.   Zero Coupon (Conditions \par         5(IV) and 6(c)): \par               (a) Amortization Yield:      5.02918688514 percent per annum \par               (b) Reference Price:         Issue Price \par               (c) Basis:                   Compounded annually \par               (d) Fixed Rate Day Count \par                Fraction(s) if not 30/360 \par                basis:                      30/360 \par  13.   Redemption Amount (Condition        The Redemption Amount with respect \par         6(a))::                             to each minimum Authorized Denomination \par                                             will be a JPY amount calculated \par                                             by the Calculation Agent as \par                                             of the IDR Valuation Date as \par                                             follows: \par  \par                                             minimum Authorized Denomination \par  \par                                             multiplied by \par  \par                                             the IDR Rate \par  \par                                             (and rounding, if necessary, \par                                             the entire resulting figure \par                                             to the nearest whole JPY, with \par                                             JPY 0.5 being rounded upwards). \par                                             The "IDR Rate" means the IDR/JPY \par                                             exchange rate, expressed as \par                                             the amount of JPY per one IDR, \par                                             which is calculated by the Calculation \par                                             Agent as follows: \par                                             USD/JPY Reference Rate \par                                             divided by \par                                             USD/IDR Reference Rate \par                                             (and rounding, if necessary, \par                                             the entire resulting figure \par                                             to the nearest 5 decimal places, \par                                             with JPY 0.000005 being rounded \par                                             upwards). \par                                             Where: \par                                             The "USD/JPY Reference Rate" \par                                             means the mid rate of USD/JPY, \par                                             expressed as the number of JPY \par                                             per one USD, published on the \par                                             Reuters Screen "JPNU" page (or \par                                             its successor page for the purpose \par                                             of displaying such rate) as \par                                             of 12:00 p.m., Tokyo time on \par                                             the relevant IDR Valuation Date, \par                                             as determined by the Calculation \par                                             Agent in its sole discretion \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Inter-American Development Bank Issue of Debt -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                             acting in good faith and in \par                                             a commercially reasonable manner. \par                                             In the event that no such quotation \par                                             appears on the Reuters Screen \par                                             "JPNU" page (or its successor \par                                             page for the purpose of displaying \par                                     