al Note:       Yes \par                                (c) Definitive Bearer Notes:     No, except in the limited circumstances \par                                                                  described under "Form of Notes" \par                                                                  herein and in the Prospectus \par                                (d) Individual Definitive        No \par                                 Registered Notes: \par                                (e) Registered Global Notes:     No \par  10.                      Additional Risk Factors:              As set forth in the Additional \par                                                                  Investment Considerations \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additional Information regarding the Notes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1. The language set out under the heading "Use of Proceeds" in the Prospectus shall be deleted in its entirety and replaced by the following:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "An amount equal to the net proceeds of the issue of the Notes (which proceeds may be converted into other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) shall be recorded by the Bank in a separate sub-account supporting Eligible Projects. These proceeds will be invested in accordance with the Bank's conservative liquidity investment guidelines until used to support the Bank's financing of Eligible Projects. So long as the Notes are outstanding and the account has a positive balance, the Bank shall direct an amount equal to such net proceeds to its lending projects within the fields of Education, Youth, and Employment, subject to and in accordance with the Bank's policies. The Bank shall allocate amounts from the sub-account to support the financing of Eligible Projects on a semi-annual basis.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Eligible Projects" means all projects funded, in whole or in part, by the Bank that promote early childhood care and education, through formal primary and secondary education, or facilitate labor market placement by improving the transition from school to work through vocational training. Eligible Projects may include projects in Latin America and the Caribbean that target (a) early childhood development, effective teaching and learning among children and youth ("Education Projects"), (b) early childhood care and youth-at-risk programs ("Youth Projects") or (c) labor intermediation systems, job opportunities and workforce skills ("Employment Projects").\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Examples of Education Projects include, without limitation: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --           Early childhood development programs \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Primary education programs, which includes teacher training, bilingual education, literacy, math and science education and school infrastructure\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Secondary education programs, which includes programs directed to improving retention and graduation, developing teaching and learning methods and providing assistance to disadvantaged children \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --           Compensatory education programs \par    --           Teacher education and effectiveness programs \par    --           E-education programs \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Examples of Youth Projects include, without limitation: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --           Support for parents and caregivers to improve quality of child care \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Youth-At-Risk programs which support \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , policy design, and/or impact evaluations to benefit at-risk youth\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Examples of Employment Projects include, without limitation: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    --           School-to-Work transition programs \par    --           Vocational and technical education programs \par    --           Human resources and workforce development programs \par    --           Labor intermediation systems \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -- Vocational and Workforce training programs, directed at improving social and labor acclimation for youth, unemployed adults and active workers\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The above examples of Education Projects, Youth Projects and Employment Projects are for illustrative purposes only and no assurance can be provided that disbursements for projects with these specific characteristics will be made by the Bank during the term of the Notes." \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.         Additional Investment Considerations: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Notes offered by this Pricing Supplement are complex financial instruments and may not be suitable for certain investors. Investors intending to purchase the Notes should consult with their tax and financial advisors to ensure that the intended purchase meets the investment objective before making such purchase.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are various risks associated with the Notes including, but not limited to, exchange rate risk, price risk and liquidity risk. Investors should consult with their own financial, legal and accounting advisors about the risks associated with an investment in these Notes, the appropriate tools to analyze that investment, and the suitability of the investment in each investor's particular circumstances. Holders of the Notes should also consult with their professional tax advisors regarding tax laws applicable to them.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment of the Redemption Amount will be based on the IDR Rate, which is a measure of the rate of exchange between the Indonesian Rupiah and the JPY. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates are volatile and will affect the holder's return. In addition, the government of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can from time to time \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. These \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or other governmental actions could adversely affect the value of the Notes, as well as the yield (in JPY terms) on the Notes and the amount payable at maturity or upon acceleration. Even in the absence of governmental action directly affecting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, political or economic developments in Indonesia or elsewhere could lead to significant and sudden changes in the exchange rate between the Indonesian Rupiah and the JPY.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian Rupiah is an emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be subject to particularly substantial volatility, as well as to government actions including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls, devaluations and other matters which could materially and adversely affect the value of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The methodologies for determining the IDR Rate may result in a Redemption Amount (or Early Redemption Amount, as the case may be) of the Notes being significantly less than anticipated or less than what an alternative methodology for determining the IDR-JPY exchange rate would yield.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INTER-AMERICAN DEVELOPMENT BANK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Name: \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gustavo Alberto De Rosa\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Title:    Chief Financial Officer and \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Manager, Finance Department\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS, the news service of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  . RNS is approved by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Financial Conduct Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2  to act as a Primary Information Provider in the United Kingdom. Terms and conditions relating to the use and distribution of this information may apply. For further information, please contact rns@lseg.com or visit \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rns.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rns.com}}}\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 END\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IODUWAKRKOAWRAR\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 09-08-19 0600GMT\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RNS0000020190809ef890000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
