\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia c.bank\uc2  says stands ready to buy government bonds\b0\par\par\uc2 152 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2019\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Aug 7 (Reuters) - \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  "stands ready" to buy government bonds, the head of its monetary management office said on Wednesday, as financial markets in Southeast Asia's largest economy are hit by outflows due to fears of a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 already has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets this week. It also held an auction for nondeliverable forward rupiah contracts in the domestic market on Wednesday, Nanang Hendarsah said.\par \par \uc2 The auction was intended to support the rupiah, which slipped 0.2% by 0330 GMT Wednesday to 14,285 a dollar.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 10-year bond yield fell to as much as 7.618% on Wednesday, after hitting 7.729% a day before, the highest since June 11. (Reporting by Maikel Jefriando and Gayatri Suroyo; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-8-7T04:35:33.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190807ef8700cci\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
