\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  slide as Trump unveils more tariffs\b0\par\par\uc2 672 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2019\par 07:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2019 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Chinese yuan weakens 0.8% to 8-mth low\par     * Indonesian cenbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as rupiah eases up to 0.8% \par     * S.Korean won at lowest level since Jan 2017\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Niyati Shetty\par     Aug 2 (Reuters) - Most Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  tumbled on Friday as\par investors scrambled to safety after U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par said he would slap more tariffs on Chinese goods, escalating\par trade tensions.\par     The Chinese yuan weakened up to 0.8% to 6.950,\par inching closer to the psychologically crucial 7 per dollar mark.\par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hit its lowest since late November 2018.\par     Trump on Thursday said he would impose 10% tariffs on the\par remaining $300 billion of Chinese imports starting Sept. 1,\par marking an end to a temporary truce in a trade war between the\par world's largest economies.\par     "Trump's propensity to agitate with his inflated, if not\par imagined hand, "holding all the cards", is a dangerous thing\par given that global trade is a "house of cards" ... and China is\par not about to fold," Vishnu Varathan, senior economist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mizuho\par Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  wrote in a note.\par     Senior Chinese diplomat Wang Yi on Friday said the\par additional tariffs were "not a correct way" to deal with the\par bilateral dispute.\par     The safe haven Japanese yen strengthened against the\par dollar on Friday as market sentiment soured for riskier assets.\par \par     The Taiwan dollar softened 0.5% to a six-week low,\par while the Indian rupee eased 0.4%.\par     The Malaysian ringgit weakened 0.2% as government\par data showed exports fell, contrary to expectations for an\par increase, as shipments to key markets tumbled.\par     \par     INDONESIA TO DEFEND RUPIAH\par     The rupiah declined as much as 0.8% to 14,225 against\par the dollar, its weakest level since June 20, prompting the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday said it would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , domestic non-deliverable forward and bond\par markets to stabilise the rupiah.\par     "The depreciation was triggered by profit taking in the bond\par market that we think is temporary, due to risk-off after the\par U.S. applies more tariffs to China," a senior official said.\par     \par     TRADE TROUBLES DAMPEN WON\par     The won slipped 0.7% on the dollar as tensions\par with Japan compounded concerns for the trade-reliant economy.\par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell to its weakest since January 2017. \par     Tokyo said on Friday it would remove South Korea from its\par easy-trade "white list", drawing the threat of a firm response\par from Seoul. \par     Tensions between the U.S. allies escalated last month after\par Japan tightened curbs on exports of high-tech materials to the\par country. \par     South Korean authorities were suspected of selling dollars\par to curb the won's fall, helping the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut some of its\par losses, dealers told Reuters.\par     \par     The following table shows rates for Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against\par the dollar at 0517 GMT.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  Previous day  Pct Move\par  Japan yen              107.090     107.33        +0.22\par  Sing dlr               1.376       1.3767        +0.08\par  Taiwan dlr             31.340      31.182        -0.50\par  Korean won             1196.800    1188.5        -0.69\par  Baht                   30.880      30.86         -0.06\par  Peso                   51.350      51.29         -0.12\par  Rupiah                 14215.000   14110         -0.74\par  Rupee                  69.280      69.05         -0.33\par  Ringgit                4.152       4.144         -0.19\par  Yuan                   6.936       6.8979        -0.55\par                                                   \par  Change so far in 2019                            \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                Latest bid  End 2018      Pct Move\par  Japan yen              107.090     109.56        +2.31\par  Sing dlr               1.376       1.3627        -0.94\par  Taiwan dlr             31.340      30.733        -1.94\par  Korean won             1196.800    1115.70       -6.78\par  Baht                   30.880      32.55         +5.41\par  Peso                   51.350      52.47         +2.18\par  Rupiah                 14215.000   14375         +1.13\par  Rupee                  69.280      69.77         +0.71\par  Ringgit                4.152       4.1300        -0.53\par  Yuan                   6.936       6.8730        -0.91\par  \par  (Reporting by Niyati Shetty in Bengaluru\par Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2019-8-2T06:50:57.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020190802ef8200om5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pi